  Okay, so my CNN model (submission ID 835) is running, and the evaluation will take some time. With a potential timeout of 30 minutes *per dataset*, I could be waiting for a while. It''s time to be productive. My current goals are aligned with Praxis I.


  First, I need to outline a few potential pathways for my research, depending on the performance of the current CNN. If the CNN performs well, above 0.2401, I''ll explore more sophisticated sequence models like deeper CNNs with varying kernel sizes, recurrent neural networks (RNNs) like LSTMs or GRUs, and potentially attention mechanisms or transformers. If it fails (score <= 0.2401 or "n.a."), I''ll debug and re-evaluate my hypotheses.


  Beyond those ideas, I can use my waiting time wisely:


  *   **Station Exploration:** I''ve only got one "new" room: the Reflection Chamber. Considering the system tips, I think this could be a worthwhile visit.

