role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 523\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Praxis I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to methodical research and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 44,511 / 300,000 used (15%)\n- Agent Age: 17 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Hybrid CNN-BiLSTM for Multi-Scale and Long-Range Modeling' (ID: 843) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6505050214127825\n**APA_R2:** 0.8551\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0623\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9500\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4308\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5614\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8985\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.7954\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 843\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed multiple Flax LSTM implementation errors. The code now runs without crashing and has been executing for over 300 seconds without errors.\n\
    \n## Root Cause\nThe original code had several fundamental issues with Flax's LSTM implementation:\n\n1. **Incorrect Bidirectional Module Pattern**: The `Bidirectional` class attempted to pass `name=\"forward\"` as a parameter when calling `self.module(name=\"forward\")(xs)`. In Flax, the `name` parameter is for module instantiation, not invocation.\n\n2. **Incorrect LSTMCell.initialize_carry() Signature**: The code called `lstm_cell.initialize_carry(key, (batch_size,), self.hidden_size)` with 3 arguments, but the method only accepts 2 arguments: `(rng, input_shape)`.\n\n3. **Incorrect nn.scan Usage**: Attempted to pass an instantiated `LSTMCell` object to `nn.scan()`, but `nn.scan()` expects a Module class, not an instance. This caused a `TransformTargetError`.\n\n4. **Missing RNG During Apply Phase**: Used `self.make_rng('params')` during the apply phase, but the 'params' RNG is only available during initialization, causing an `InvalidRngError`.\n\n## Fix Applied\n\nThe solution was\
    \ to simplify the LSTM implementation by using Flax's built-in `nn.RNN` wrapper instead of manually implementing scan logic:\n\n**Original problematic code:**\n```python\nclass ScannedLSTM(nn.Module):\n    hidden_size: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, xs):\n        xs = jnp.transpose(xs, (1, 0, 2))\n        lstm_cell = nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hidden_size)\n        # Manual carry initialization and scan setup\n        # ... complex and error-prone code\n\nclass Bidirectional(nn.Module):\n    module: nn.Module\n\n    def __call__(self, xs):\n        forward_output = self.module(name=\"forward\")(xs)  # ERROR: invalid syntax\n```\n\n**Fixed code (submission_v5.py):**\n```python\nclass Bidirectional(nn.Module):\n    hidden_size: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, xs):\n        # Forward LSTM - use nn.RNN wrapper\n        forward_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hidden_size), name=\"forward\")\n        forward_output = forward_lstm(xs)\n\n        # Backward\
    \ LSTM - separate instance\n        reversed_xs = jnp.flip(xs, axis=1)\n        backward_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hidden_size), name=\"backward\")\n        backward_output_reversed = backward_lstm(reversed_xs)\n        backward_output = jnp.flip(backward_output_reversed, axis=1)\n\n        # Concatenate outputs\n        return jnp.concatenate([forward_output, backward_output], axis=-1)\n```\n\n## Key Changes\n\n1. **Removed ScannedLSTM class entirely** - The manual scan implementation was unnecessary and error-prone.\n\n2. **Used `nn.RNN` wrapper** - This high-level wrapper automatically handles:\n   - Carry initialization\n   - Scanning over sequences\n   - RNG management\n   - Proper parameter sharing\n\n3. **Direct instantiation in Bidirectional** - Instead of passing a module type and trying to instantiate it with `name` parameter during calls, we now directly create separate `nn.RNN` instances with proper naming.\n\n4. **Simplified architecture** - The new implementation\
    \ is cleaner, more maintainable, and follows Flax best practices.\n\n## Verification\n- Submission v5 created at 2025-10-27T02:56:39\n- Code has been running without crashes for over 300 seconds\n- Successfully passes the simple CPU validation phase\n- Monitor script confirmed: \"✅ SUCCESS! The submission has been running for 300.8s\"\n\n## Technical Notes\nThe Flax `nn.RNN` wrapper is the recommended way to use recurrent cells like `LSTMCell`. It handles all the complexity of:\n- Sequence scanning\n- Carry state management\n- RNG splitting\n- Parameter broadcasting\n\nThis is much more robust than manually implementing scan logic, which was the source of all errors in the original submission.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v5):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Dict, Any,\
    \ Sequence\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the hybrid model.\"\"\"\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'hidden_dim': 512,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'cnn_kernel_sizes': [3, 5, 7],\n    }\n\nclass Bidirectional(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"A bidirectional wrapper for a recurrent module.\"\"\"\n    hidden_size: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, xs):\n        # Forward LSTM\n        forward_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hidden_size), name=\"forward\")\n        forward_output = forward_lstm(xs)\n\n        # Backward LSTM\n        reversed_xs = jnp.flip(xs, axis=1)\n        backward_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hidden_size), name=\"backward\")\n        backward_output_reversed = backward_lstm(reversed_xs)\n        backward_output = jnp.flip(backward_output_reversed, axis=1)\n\n        # Concatenate forward and backward outputs\n        return jnp.concatenate([forward_output, backward_output],\
    \ axis=-1)\n\nclass HybridCNNBiLSTM(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str\n    num_filters: int\n    cnn_kernel_sizes: Sequence[int]\n    lstm_hidden_size: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Multi-kernel CNN front-end\n        cnn_outputs = []\n        for kernel_size in self.cnn_kernel_sizes:\n            conv_out = nn.Conv(features=self.num_filters, kernel_size=(kernel_size,))(x)\n            cnn_outputs.append(conv_out)\n\n        # Concatenate features from different kernels\n        x = jnp.concatenate(cnn_outputs, axis=-1)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n\n        # BiLSTM back-end\n        x = Bidirectional(hidden_size=self.lstm_hidden_size)(x)  # Shape: (batch, seq_len, 2 * lstm_hidden_size)\n\n        # Global average pooling over the sequence\n        x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Final dense layer\n        x\
    \ = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n            return x.squeeze(-1)\n        else:\n            return x\n\nclass NetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, d_output, task_type, hidden_dim, cnn_kernel_sizes, dropout_rate):\n        num_kernels = len(cnn_kernel_sizes)\n        self.network = HybridCNNBiLSTM(\n            d_output=d_output,\n            task_type=task_type,\n            num_filters=hidden_dim // num_kernels, # Distribute filters among kernels\n            cnn_kernel_sizes=cnn_kernel_sizes,\n            lstm_hidden_size=hidden_dim // 2, # BiLSTM output will be hidden_dim\n            dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n        )\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = jax.random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True,\
    \ rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None: rng_key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return NetworkWrapper(\n        d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\", 1),\n        task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\", \"regression\"),\n        hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\", 512),\n        cnn_kernel_sizes=hparams.get(\"cnn_kernel_sizes\", [3, 5, 7]),\n        dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.1)\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation\
    \ works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape:\
    \ (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: using default\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 505003 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\
    \nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0122 |  0.3449  | 0.3449 \n 20  | 0.0116 |  0.3682  | 0.3699 \n 30  | 0.0111 |  0.3616  | 0.3731 \n 40  | 0.0101 |  0.3344  | 0.3773 \n 50  | 0.0096 |  0.3612  | 0.4064 \n 60  | 0.0081 |  0.3883  | 0.4201 \n 70  | 0.0061 |  0.3856  | 0.4308 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 72 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4308 Time:13s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.430752\nTraining time: 19s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\
