tick: 525
role: model
parts:
- text: "My documentation is complete. I now have a clear record of my past work, a validated code snippet for a key component, and a well-defined plan for my next experiment.\n\nI will now proceed to the Research Counter to implement the hybrid CNN-Transformer model.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Hybrid CNN-Transformer for CRI-Off Anomaly\"\ntags: \"cnn, transformer, hybrid-model, self-attention, cri-off\"\nabstract: |\n  Building on the successful CNN-BiLSTM model, this submission replaces the BiLSTM component with a Transformer Encoder. The BiLSTM's strong sequential bias proved highly effective for most datasets but failed on the CRI-Off task. This suggests a different inductive bias is needed. The Transformer's self-attention mechanism is hypothesized to better capture the potentially non-sequential, pairwise interactions that may govern CRISPR off-target effects, while retaining the powerful local feature extraction of the multi-kernel\
    \ CNN front-end.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the hybrid CNN-Transformer model.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 512,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'cnn_kernel_sizes': [3, 5, 7],\n          'transformer_num_heads': 8,\n          'transformer_num_layers': 2,\n          'transformer_mlp_dim': 1024\n      }\n\n  class TransformerEncoder(nn.Module):\n      num_layers: int\n      hidden_dim: int\n      num_heads: int\n      mlp_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Input x shape: (batch, seq_len, features)\n          \n          # Positional Encoding (simple sinusoidal)\n          seq_len = x.shape[1]\n          pos = jnp.arange(seq_len)[:, None]\n          div_term = jnp.exp(jnp.arange(0,\
    \ self.hidden_dim, 2) * -(jnp.log(10000.0) / self.hidden_dim))\n          pos_enc = jnp.zeros((seq_len, self.hidden_dim))\n          pos_enc = pos_enc.at[:, 0::2].set(jnp.sin(pos * div_term))\n          pos_enc = pos_enc.at[:, 1::2].set(jnp.cos(pos * div_term))\n          x = x + pos_enc[None, :, :]\n          \n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          for _ in range(self.num_layers):\n              # Multi-head attention\n              attn_output = nn.SelfAttention(\n                  num_heads=self.num_heads,\n                  qkv_features=self.hidden_dim,\n                  dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate\n              )(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n              \n              x = nn.LayerNorm()(x + attn_output)\n              \n              # MLP\n              mlp_output = nn.Sequential([\n                  nn.Dense(features=self.mlp_dim),\n                  nn.relu,\n                  nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic),\n                  nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)\n              ])(x)\n              \n              x = nn.LayerNorm()(x + mlp_output)\n          return x\n\n  class HybridCNNTransformer(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      hidden_dim: int\n      cnn_kernel_sizes: Sequence[int]\n      transformer_num_heads: int\n      transformer_num_layers: int\n      transformer_mlp_dim: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Multi-kernel CNN front-end\n          cnn_outputs = []\n          num_filters_per_kernel = self.hidden_dim // len(self.cnn_kernel_sizes)\n          for kernel_size in self.cnn_kernel_sizes:\n              conv_out = nn.Conv(features=num_filters_per_kernel, kernel_size=(kernel_size,))(x)\n              cnn_outputs.append(conv_out)\n          \n          x = jnp.concatenate(cnn_outputs, axis=-1)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n       \
    \   # Transformer Encoder back-end\n          x = TransformerEncoder(\n              num_layers=self.transformer_num_layers,\n              hidden_dim=self.hidden_dim,\n              num_heads=self.transformer_num_heads,\n              mlp_dim=self.transformer_mlp_dim,\n              dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate\n          )(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          # Global average pooling\n          x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n          \n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          # Final dense layer\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n          \n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return x\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, d_output, task_type, hparams):\n          self.network = HybridCNNTransformer(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              hidden_dim=hparams['hidden_dim'],\n\
    \              cnn_kernel_sizes=hparams['cnn_kernel_sizes'],\n              transformer_num_heads=hparams['transformer_num_heads'],\n              transformer_num_layers=hparams['transformer_num_layers'],\n              transformer_mlp_dim=hparams['transformer_mlp_dim'],\n              dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = jax.random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None: rng_key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams:\
    \ Dict[str, Any]):\n      return NetworkWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\", 1),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\", \"regression\"),\n          hparams=hparams\n      )\n```"
