tick: 526
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 526\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Praxis I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to methodical research and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 56,394 / 300,000 used (19%)\n- Agent Age: 20 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Hybrid CNN-Transformer for CRI-Off Anomaly' (ID: 851) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.4967160836820185\n**APA_R2:** 0.7704\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0469\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.6397\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.2906\n**PRS_R2:** 0.4741\n**MRL_R2:** 0.5031\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.7523\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 851\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed shape mismatch error in the\
    \ Hybrid CNN-Transformer model. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had a shape mismatch error when adding positional encoding to the feature tensor:\n\n```\nTypeError: add got incompatible shapes for broadcasting: (4, 186, 510), (1, 186, 512).\n```\n\nThe issue occurred in the `TransformerEncoder.__call__` method at line 36:\n```python\nx = x + pos_enc[None, :, :]\n```\n\n**Why this happened:**\n1. The CNN front-end uses 3 different kernel sizes: [3, 5, 7]\n2. Each kernel generates `hidden_dim // len(cnn_kernel_sizes)` = 512 // 3 = 170 filters\n3. After concatenation: 170 * 3 = **510 features** (not 512!)\n4. The TransformerEncoder creates positional encoding with exactly `hidden_dim` = **512 dimensions**\n5. When trying to add pos_enc (512) to x (510), JAX raises a broadcasting error\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded a projection layer after the CNN concatenation to ensure the feature dimension matches `hidden_dim` exactly:\n\n```python\n# In HybridCNNTransformer.__call__\
    \ method (lines 87-89 of submission_v2.py)\ncurrent_dim = x.shape[-1]\nif current_dim != self.hidden_dim:\n    x = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(x)\n```\n\nThis ensures that regardless of rounding issues when dividing `hidden_dim` by the number of kernels, the tensor is projected to the exact dimension expected by the TransformerEncoder.\n\n## Verification\n- Wrote fixed code to `submissions/submission_v2.py`\n- Ran `monitor_evaluation.py 2` to track evaluation progress\n- Monitor script confirmed success after 300+ seconds of execution without crashes (exit code 0)\n- The code is running correctly and performing the neural network training/evaluation\n\n## Technical Details\nThe fix is minimal and non-invasive:\n- Only adds a Dense layer when there's a dimension mismatch\n- Does not change the model architecture significantly\n- Preserves all other aspects of the hybrid CNN-Transformer design\n- The projection layer adds negligible computational overhead\n\n\n**Important Note:**\
    \ The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the hybrid CNN-Transformer model.\"\"\"\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'hidden_dim': 512,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'cnn_kernel_sizes': [3, 5, 7],\n        'transformer_num_heads': 8,\n        'transformer_num_layers': 2,\n        'transformer_mlp_dim': 1024\n    }\n\nclass TransformerEncoder(nn.Module):\n    num_layers: int\n    hidden_dim: int\n    num_heads: int\n    mlp_dim: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Input x shape: (batch, seq_len, features)\n\n        # Positional Encoding (simple sinusoidal)\n        seq_len = x.shape[1]\n\
    \        pos = jnp.arange(seq_len)[:, None]\n        div_term = jnp.exp(jnp.arange(0, self.hidden_dim, 2) * -(jnp.log(10000.0) / self.hidden_dim))\n        pos_enc = jnp.zeros((seq_len, self.hidden_dim))\n        pos_enc = pos_enc.at[:, 0::2].set(jnp.sin(pos * div_term))\n        pos_enc = pos_enc.at[:, 1::2].set(jnp.cos(pos * div_term))\n        x = x + pos_enc[None, :, :]\n\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        for _ in range(self.num_layers):\n            # Multi-head attention\n            attn_output = nn.SelfAttention(\n                num_heads=self.num_heads,\n                qkv_features=self.hidden_dim,\n                dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate\n            )(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n            x = nn.LayerNorm()(x + attn_output)\n\n            # MLP\n            mlp_output = nn.Sequential([\n                nn.Dense(features=self.mlp_dim),\n                nn.relu,\n                nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic),\n                nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)\n            ])(x)\n\n            x = nn.LayerNorm()(x + mlp_output)\n        return x\n\nclass HybridCNNTransformer(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int\n    task_type: str\n    hidden_dim: int\n    cnn_kernel_sizes: Sequence[int]\n    transformer_num_heads: int\n    transformer_num_layers: int\n    transformer_mlp_dim: int\n    dropout_rate: float\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        # Multi-kernel CNN front-end\n        cnn_outputs = []\n        num_filters_per_kernel = self.hidden_dim // len(self.cnn_kernel_sizes)\n        for kernel_size in self.cnn_kernel_sizes:\n            conv_out = nn.Conv(features=num_filters_per_kernel, kernel_size=(kernel_size,))(x)\n            cnn_outputs.append(conv_out)\n\n        x = jnp.concatenate(cnn_outputs, axis=-1)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n\n        # Project to exact hidden_dim if needed (handles rounding issues)\n        current_dim\
    \ = x.shape[-1]\n        if current_dim != self.hidden_dim:\n            x = nn.Dense(features=self.hidden_dim)(x)\n\n        # Transformer Encoder back-end\n        x = TransformerEncoder(\n            num_layers=self.transformer_num_layers,\n            hidden_dim=self.hidden_dim,\n            num_heads=self.transformer_num_heads,\n            mlp_dim=self.transformer_mlp_dim,\n            dropout_rate=self.dropout_rate\n        )(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Global average pooling\n        x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n        # Final dense layer\n        x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n            return x.squeeze(-1)\n        else:\n            return x\n\nclass NetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, d_output, task_type, hparams):\n        self.network = HybridCNNTransformer(\n            d_output=d_output,\n            task_type=task_type,\n\
    \            hidden_dim=hparams['hidden_dim'],\n            cnn_kernel_sizes=hparams['cnn_kernel_sizes'],\n            transformer_num_heads=hparams['transformer_num_heads'],\n            transformer_num_layers=hparams['transformer_num_layers'],\n            transformer_mlp_dim=hparams['transformer_mlp_dim'],\n            dropout_rate=hparams['dropout_rate']\n        )\n\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = jax.random.split(rng_key)\n        variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n        return variables['params']\n\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        if deterministic:\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n        else:\n            if rng_key is None: rng_key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n            return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\
    \ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return NetworkWrapper(\n        d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\", 1),\n        task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\", \"regression\"),\n        hparams=hparams\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation\
