tick: 529
role: model
parts:
- text: "My plan is now documented. I will proceed to the Research Counter to implement the CNN-BiLSTM model with an attention mechanism. I will use my validated BiLSTM code from my private memory as a starting point.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"CNN-BiLSTM with Attention Mechanism\"\ntags: \"cnn, lstm, attention, hybrid-model, cri-off\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission modifies the high-performing CNN-BiLSTM model (ID 843) by replacing the final mean pooling layer with an additive attention mechanism. The previous model struggled on the CRI-Off dataset, suggesting that global context can be noisy for some tasks. The attention layer allows the model to learn a weighted average of the BiLSTM's output states, enabling it to focus on the most salient features for a given sequence and task. This is hypothesized to improve performance on noisy datasets like CRI-Off without degrading performance on tasks where global context is important.\n\
    content: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"Define hyperparameters for the hybrid model.\"\"\"\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 512,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'cnn_kernel_sizes': [3, 5, 7],\n      }\n\n  class Bidirectional(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Validated BiLSTM wrapper from debugger report (ID 843).\"\"\"\n      hidden_size: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, xs):\n          forward_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hidden_size), name=\"forward\")\n          forward_output = forward_lstm(xs)\n          \n          reversed_xs = jnp.flip(xs, axis=1)\n          backward_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hidden_size), name=\"backward\")\n          backward_output_reversed = backward_lstm(reversed_xs)\n          backward_output = jnp.flip(backward_output_reversed, axis=1)\n\
    \          \n          return jnp.concatenate([forward_output, backward_output], axis=-1)\n\n  class Attention(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Simple additive attention layer.\"\"\"\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          # x shape: (batch, seq_len, features)\n          features = x.shape[-1]\n          \n          # Attention weights\n          attention_weights = nn.Dense(features=features, name='attention_w')(x)\n          attention_weights = nn.tanh(attention_weights)\n          attention_weights = nn.Dense(features=1, name='attention_v')(attention_weights)\n          attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_weights, axis=1)\n          \n          # Weighted sum\n          context_vector = jnp.sum(x * attention_weights, axis=1)\n          return context_vector\n\n  class HybridCNNAttentionBiLSTM(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      num_filters: int\n      cnn_kernel_sizes: Sequence[int]\n      lstm_hidden_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\
    \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          # Multi-kernel CNN front-end\n          cnn_outputs = []\n          for kernel_size in self.cnn_kernel_sizes:\n              conv_out = nn.Conv(features=self.num_filters, kernel_size=(kernel_size,))(x)\n              cnn_outputs.append(conv_out)\n          \n          x = jnp.concatenate(cnn_outputs, axis=-1)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # BiLSTM back-end\n          x = Bidirectional(hidden_size=self.lstm_hidden_size)(x)\n          \n          # Attention layer instead of mean pooling\n          x = Attention()(x)\n          \n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          \n          # Final dense layer\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n          \n          if self.task_type == \"regression\":\n              return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              return x\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self,\
    \ d_output, task_type, hidden_dim, cnn_kernel_sizes, dropout_rate):\n          num_kernels = len(cnn_kernel_sizes)\n          self.network = HybridCNNAttentionBiLSTM(\n              d_output=d_output,\n              task_type=task_type,\n              num_filters=hidden_dim // num_kernels,\n              cnn_kernel_sizes=cnn_kernel_sizes,\n              lstm_hidden_size=hidden_dim // 2,\n              dropout_rate=dropout_rate\n          )\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = jax.random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None: rng_key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return\
    \ self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return NetworkWrapper(\n          d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\", 1),\n          task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\", \"regression\"),\n          hidden_dim=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\", 512),\n          cnn_kernel_sizes=hparams.get(\"cnn_kernel_sizes\", [3, 5, 7]),\n          dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.1)\n      )\n```"
