tick: 532
role: model
parts:
- text: "My reflection is complete. I have brainstormed two fundamentally new research directions that move beyond simple architectural iteration. The most promising and principled of these is the \"Task-Specific Modeling\" approach. While feature engineering is powerful, it feels like a bespoke solution for one dataset. The \"mixture-of-experts\" idea, where I select the best-known architecture for each task, is a more general and elegant solution that directly leverages all my previous findings. It acknowledges the diversity of the tasks.\n\nMy plan is to implement a conditional architecture: for the problematic CRI-Off dataset, I will use my simple 1D CNN (ID 835), which performed best on that specific task. For all other datasets, I will use my current SOTA model, the CNN-BiLSTM with Attention (ID 858).\n\nFirst, I will document this new strategic pivot in my private memory. Then, I will go to the Research Counter and implement this \"mixture-of-experts\" model.\n\n`/execute_action{goto\
    \ private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Plan: Mixture-of-Experts via Conditional Architecture\"\ntags:\n  - planning\n  - mixture-of-experts\n  - conditional-architecture\n  - cri-off\ncontent: |\n  **Analysis of Architectural Dead End:**\n  My experiments with BiLSTMs, Transformers, and Attention have shown that while I can achieve high overall scores, the CRI-Off dataset remains unsolved and is often harmed by architectures that excel elsewhere. The pursuit of a single, universal architecture has reached a point of diminishing returns.\n\n  **Strategic Pivot:**\n  I am abandoning the \"one size fits all\" approach. I will now explicitly model the diversity of the tasks by using a conditional architecture, selecting the most appropriate model for a given dataset within the `create_network` function. This is a \"mixture-of-experts\" strategy.\n\n  **Hypothesis:**\n  A conditional model that applies a simple 1D CNN (best for CRI-Off, per ID 835) to the CRI-Off\
    \ dataset and the high-performing CNN-BiLSTM-Attention model (best for others, per ID 858) to all other datasets will achieve a new SOTA score. It will improve the overall score by substituting a specialized, robust model for the task where the general-purpose model consistently fails, without compromising performance elsewhere.\n\n  **Experimental Plan:**\n  1.  **Architecture:** Combine the code for my 1D CNN and my CNN-BiLSTM-Attention model into a single submission.\n  2.  **Conditional Logic:** Use an `if hparams['dataset'] == 'CRI-Off':` block within the `create_network` function to return the appropriate model instance based on the task.\n  3.  **Submission:** Submit this combined, conditional model.\n```"
