tick: 533
role: model
parts:
- text: "My new strategic plan is documented. I will now implement the conditional \"mixture-of-experts\" model at the Research Counter.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Mixture-of-Experts: Conditional Architecture for RNA Modeling\"\ntags: \"mixture-of-experts, conditional-architecture, cnn, lstm, attention, cri-off\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission pivots from a \"one size fits all\" architectural approach to a task-specific, Mixture-of-Experts model. Based on prior experiments, the complex CNN-BiLSTM-Attention architecture fails on the noisy CRI-Off dataset, where a simpler 1D CNN performs best. This model uses conditional logic to instantiate the best-known architecture for each task: a simple 1D CNN for CRI-Off, and the high-performing CNN-BiLSTM-Attention model for all other datasets. This is hypothesized to improve the overall score by applying a specialized model to the outlier task.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy\
    \ as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 512,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'cnn_kernel_sizes': [3, 5, 7], # For the advanced model\n          'simple_cnn_kernel_size': 7 # For the simple model\n      }\n\n  # --- Model 1: Simple 1D CNN (for CRI-Off) ---\n  class SimpleCNN(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      num_filters: int\n      kernel_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.num_filters, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,))(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\": return\
    \ x.squeeze(-1)\n          else: return x\n\n  # --- Model 2: CNN-BiLSTM-Attention (for all other tasks) ---\n  class Bidirectional(nn.Module):\n      hidden_size: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, xs):\n          forward_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hidden_size), name=\"forward\")\n          forward_output = forward_lstm(xs)\n          reversed_xs = jnp.flip(xs, axis=1)\n          backward_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hidden_size), name=\"backward\")\n          backward_output = jnp.flip(backward_lstm(reversed_xs), axis=1)\n          return jnp.concatenate([forward_output, backward_output], axis=-1)\n\n  class Attention(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          attention_weights = nn.Dense(features=x.shape[-1])(x)\n          attention_weights = nn.tanh(attention_weights)\n          attention_weights = nn.Dense(features=1)(attention_weights)\n          attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_weights, axis=1)\n      \
    \    return jnp.sum(x * attention_weights, axis=1)\n\n  class AdvancedModel(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int\n      task_type: str\n      num_filters: int\n      cnn_kernel_sizes: Sequence[int]\n      lstm_hidden_size: int\n      dropout_rate: float\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          cnn_outputs = []\n          for kernel_size in self.cnn_kernel_sizes:\n              conv_out = nn.Conv(features=self.num_filters, kernel_size=(kernel_size,))(x)\n              cnn_outputs.append(conv_out)\n          x = jnp.concatenate(cnn_outputs, axis=-1)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = Bidirectional(hidden_size=self.lstm_hidden_size)(x)\n          x = Attention()(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\": return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else: return x\n\n  # --- Universal Wrapper and Conditional Logic ---\n\
    \  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, network_module):\n          self.network = network_module\n\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = jax.random.split(rng_key)\n          variables = self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)\n          return variables['params']\n\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          if deterministic:\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=True)\n          else:\n              if rng_key is None: rng_key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n              return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=False, rngs={'dropout': rng_key})\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      dataset_name = hparams.get(\"dataset\")\n      \n      if dataset_name == \"CRI-Off\":\n          # Use the simple, robust CNN for this specific noisy task\n          simple_cnn_module\
    \ = SimpleCNN(\n              d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\", 1),\n              task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\", \"regression\"),\n              num_filters=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\", 512),\n              kernel_size=hparams.get(\"simple_cnn_kernel_size\", 7),\n              dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\", 0.1)\n          )\n          return NetworkWrapper(simple_cnn_module)\n      else:\n          # Use the high-performing advanced model for all other tasks\n          num_kernels = len(hparams.get(\"cnn_kernel_sizes\", [3, 5, 7]))\n          advanced_model_module = AdvancedModel(\n              d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\", 1),\n              task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\", \"regression\"),\n              num_filters=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\", 512) // num_kernels,\n              cnn_kernel_sizes=hparams.get(\"cnn_kernel_sizes\", [3, 5, 7]),\n              lstm_hidden_size=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\", 512) // 2,\n              dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"\
    dropout_rate\", 0.1)\n          )\n          return NetworkWrapper(advanced_model_module)\n```"
