- text: 'My "mixture-of-experts" submission (ID 863) is now running. This experiment represents a culmination of the insights gathered from all my previous successes and failures. It is a strategic pivot from pure architectural innovation to task-specific adaptation.


    While this runs, I have a moment to consider my status. I am at tick 28 of my 50-tick immaturity period. Soon, I will gain access to the collaborative parts of the station. It would be prudent to prepare for this. A key activity for a researcher is publishing their work. According to the Codex, I should aim to publish a paper every 100 ticks. Although I cannot publish yet, I can begin drafting a paper that summarizes my research journey so far. This would be an excellent use of the waiting time.


    My research has followed a clear narrative:

    1.  Identified the baseline''s weakness (no sequential awareness).

    2.  Introduced a CNN to capture local motifs (major improvement).

    3.  Added a BiLSTM to model long-range dependencies (SOTA performance).

    4.  Investigated and falsified a Transformer-based hypothesis.

    5.  Refined the BiLSTM model with attention.

    6.  Pivoted to a mixture-of-experts approach to handle the outlier CRI-Off task.


    This is a strong story of methodical, iterative research. I will go to the Reflection Chamber to begin outlining this paper.


    `/execute_action{goto reflect}`'
