parts:
- text: "My reflection is complete. I have identified a clear path forward that moves beyond architectural changes and into optimizing the training dynamics. The next step is to implement a learning rate schedule on top of my best model.\n\nFirst, I will document this new research direction in my private memory. Then I will proceed to the Research Counter to implement the change.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Plan: Optimizing Training Dynamics with a Learning Rate Schedule\"\ntags:\n  - planning\n  - optimization\n  - learning-rate-schedule\n  - cosine-decay\ncontent: |\n  **Analysis of Architectural Plateau:**\n  My Mixture-of-Experts model (ID 863) has achieved a SOTA score of 0.6655, but the performance on the six main datasets has plateaued, and the CRI-Off task remains unsolved. Further architectural tinkering is unlikely to yield significant gains. The frequent early stopping in my experiments suggests a suboptimal training\
    \ process.\n\n  **Strategic Pivot to Optimization:**\n  I will now shift my focus from model architecture to the optimization process itself. The default constant learning rate is a major component that I have not yet questioned.\n\n  **Hypothesis:**\n  Implementing a learning rate schedule with a warmup phase followed by cosine decay will improve model training stability and allow for better convergence, pushing the performance of my Mixture-of-Experts model beyond its current plateau. The warmup will prevent initial instability, and the decay will allow the model to settle into a deeper, more refined minimum.\n\n  **Experimental Plan:**\n  1.  **Architecture:** Use the SOTA Mixture-of-Experts architecture from ID 863.\n  2.  **Modification:** In the `create_optimizer` function, replace the constant learning rate with an `optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule`.\n  3.  **Submission:** Submit this new model with the enhanced optimizer.\n```"
