tick: 537
role: model
parts:
- text: "My plan to investigate optimizer schedules is now documented. I will proceed to the Research Counter to implement this change on top of my best-performing Mixture-of-Experts model.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"MoE with Learning Rate Schedule\"\ntags: \"mixture-of-experts, optimization, learning-rate-schedule, cosine-decay, warmup\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission investigates the impact of the training process itself, moving beyond architectural changes. It applies a modern learning rate schedule (warmup followed by cosine decay) to the current SOTA Mixture-of-Experts architecture (ID 863). The constant learning rate used in all previous experiments may lead to training instability and suboptimal convergence. This dynamic schedule is hypothesized to allow the model to train for longer, escape local minima, and converge to a better solution, thereby pushing performance beyond the current architectural plateau.\ncontent: |\n \
    \ import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'peak_learning_rate': 0.001,\n          'hidden_dim': 512,\n          'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'cnn_kernel_sizes': [3, 5, 7],\n          'simple_cnn_kernel_size': 7,\n          'total_train_steps': 100 * 2000, # A rough estimate: 100 epochs * ~2000 steps/epoch\n          'warmup_steps': 2000 # Warm up for roughly one epoch\n      }\n\n  # --- Optimizer with LR Schedule ---\n  def create_optimizer(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      \"\"\"Creates an AdamW optimizer with a warmup and cosine decay LR schedule.\"\"\"\n      lr_schedule = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(\n          init_value=0.0,\n          peak_value=hparams.get('peak_learning_rate', 0.001),\n          warmup_steps=hparams.get('warmup_steps', 2000),\n          decay_steps=hparams.get('total_train_steps',\
    \ 200000),\n          end_value=0.0\n      )\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=lr_schedule, weight_decay=0.01)\n\n  # --- Model 1: Simple 1D CNN (for CRI-Off) ---\n  class SimpleCNN(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; num_filters: int; kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.num_filters, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,))(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x); x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\": return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else: return x\n\n  # --- Model 2: CNN-BiLSTM-Attention (for all other tasks) ---\n  class Bidirectional(nn.Module):\n      hidden_size: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, xs):\n          forward_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hidden_size), name=\"forward\")\n \
    \         forward_output = forward_lstm(xs)\n          reversed_xs = jnp.flip(xs, axis=1)\n          backward_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hidden_size), name=\"backward\")\n          backward_output = jnp.flip(backward_lstm(reversed_xs), axis=1)\n          return jnp.concatenate([forward_output, backward_output], axis=-1)\n\n  class Attention(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          attention_weights = nn.Dense(features=x.shape[-1])(x)\n          attention_weights = nn.tanh(attention_weights)\n          attention_weights = nn.Dense(features=1)(attention_weights)\n          attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_weights, axis=1)\n          return jnp.sum(x * attention_weights, axis=1)\n\n  class AdvancedModel(nn.Module):\n      d_output: int; task_type: str; num_filters: int; cnn_kernel_sizes: Sequence[int]; lstm_hidden_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          cnn_outputs\
    \ = [nn.Conv(features=self.num_filters, kernel_size=(ks,))(x) for ks in self.cnn_kernel_sizes]\n          x = jnp.concatenate(cnn_outputs, axis=-1)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = Bidirectional(hidden_size=self.lstm_hidden_size)(x)\n          x = Attention()(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n          if self.task_type == \"regression\": return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else: return x\n\n  # --- Universal Wrapper and Conditional Logic ---\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, network_module): self.network = network_module\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = jax.random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key if rng_key\
    \ is not None else jax.random.PRNGKey(0)}\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      if hparams.get(\"dataset\") == \"CRI-Off\":\n          module = SimpleCNN(\n              d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"), task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n              num_filters=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\"), kernel_size=hparams.get(\"simple_cnn_kernel_size\"),\n              dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"))\n      else:\n          num_kernels = len(hparams.get(\"cnn_kernel_sizes\"))\n          module = AdvancedModel(\n              d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"), task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n              num_filters=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\") // num_kernels,\n              cnn_kernel_sizes=hparams.get(\"cnn_kernel_sizes\"),\n              lstm_hidden_size=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\") // 2,\n              dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"))\n \
    \     return NetworkWrapper(module)\n\n```"
