role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 539\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Praxis I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to methodical research and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 91,970 / 300,000 used (31%)\n- Agent Age: 33 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'MoE with Learning Rate Schedule' (ID: 869) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.6668748773219358\n**APA_R2:** 0.8544\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0770\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9498\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4273\n**PRS_R2:** 0.5509\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8903\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9185\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 869\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the function signature mismatch in `create_optimizer()`. The code now runs without crashing for over 300 seconds.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission defined\
    \ `create_optimizer()` with the wrong parameter signature:\n\n```python\ndef create_optimizer(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    lr_schedule = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(\n        init_value=0.0,\n        peak_value=hparams.get('peak_learning_rate', 0.001),  # Error: hparams is a float!\n        ...\n    )\n```\n\nHowever, the evaluation system's `main.py` calls this function with a single `learning_rate` float:\n\n```python\noptimizer = funcs['create_optimizer'](learning_rate)  # learning_rate is a float\n```\n\nThis caused an `AttributeError: 'float' object has no attribute 'get'` when the function tried to call `hparams.get()`.\n\nThe default implementation signature is:\n```python\ndef default_create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001) -> optax.GradientTransformation\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged the function signature to match the expected interface:\n\n1. **Updated parameter**: Changed from `hparams: Dict[str, Any]` to `learning_rate: float = 0.001`\n2. **Internal call**:\
    \ Added a call to `_define_hyperparameters()` inside the function to get the schedule parameters\n3. **Preserved functionality**: The learning rate schedule logic remains unchanged\n\n```python\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    \"\"\"Creates an AdamW optimizer with a warmup and cosine decay LR schedule.\"\"\"\n    # Get hyperparameters to access schedule parameters\n    hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n\n    lr_schedule = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(\n        init_value=0.0,\n        peak_value=hparams.get('peak_learning_rate', learning_rate),\n        warmup_steps=hparams.get('warmup_steps', 2000),\n        decay_steps=hparams.get('total_train_steps', 200000),\n        end_value=0.0\n    )\n    return optax.adamw(learning_rate=lr_schedule, weight_decay=0.01)\n```\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that submission v2 runs successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing (exit code 0). The code is now executing the training loop with\
    \ the warmup and cosine decay learning rate schedule as intended.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n# --- Hyperparameters ---\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'peak_learning_rate': 0.001,\n        'hidden_dim': 512,\n        'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n        'cnn_kernel_sizes': [3, 5, 7],\n        'simple_cnn_kernel_size': 7,\n        'total_train_steps': 100 * 2000, # A rough estimate: 100 epochs * ~2000 steps/epoch\n        'warmup_steps': 2000 # Warm up for roughly one epoch\n    }\n\n# --- Optimizer with LR Schedule ---\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    \"\"\"Creates an AdamW optimizer with a warmup and cosine decay LR schedule.\"\"\"\n    # Get hyperparameters\
    \ to access schedule parameters\n    hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n\n    lr_schedule = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(\n        init_value=0.0,\n        peak_value=hparams.get('peak_learning_rate', learning_rate),\n        warmup_steps=hparams.get('warmup_steps', 2000),\n        decay_steps=hparams.get('total_train_steps', 200000),\n        end_value=0.0\n    )\n    return optax.adamw(learning_rate=lr_schedule, weight_decay=0.01)\n\n# --- Model 1: Simple 1D CNN (for CRI-Off) ---\nclass SimpleCNN(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int; task_type: str; num_filters: int; kernel_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        x = nn.Conv(features=self.num_filters, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,))(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x); x = jnp.mean(x, axis=1)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\": return x.squeeze(-1)\n\
    \        else: return x\n\n# --- Model 2: CNN-BiLSTM-Attention (for all other tasks) ---\nclass Bidirectional(nn.Module):\n    hidden_size: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, xs):\n        forward_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hidden_size), name=\"forward\")\n        forward_output = forward_lstm(xs)\n        reversed_xs = jnp.flip(xs, axis=1)\n        backward_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hidden_size), name=\"backward\")\n        backward_output = jnp.flip(backward_lstm(reversed_xs), axis=1)\n        return jnp.concatenate([forward_output, backward_output], axis=-1)\n\nclass Attention(nn.Module):\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        attention_weights = nn.Dense(features=x.shape[-1])(x)\n        attention_weights = nn.tanh(attention_weights)\n        attention_weights = nn.Dense(features=1)(attention_weights)\n        attention_weights = nn.softmax(attention_weights, axis=1)\n        return jnp.sum(x * attention_weights, axis=1)\n\nclass\
    \ AdvancedModel(nn.Module):\n    d_output: int; task_type: str; num_filters: int; cnn_kernel_sizes: Sequence[int]; lstm_hidden_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        cnn_outputs = [nn.Conv(features=self.num_filters, kernel_size=(ks,))(x) for ks in self.cnn_kernel_sizes]\n        x = jnp.concatenate(cnn_outputs, axis=-1)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = Bidirectional(hidden_size=self.lstm_hidden_size)(x)\n        x = Attention()(x)\n        x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n        x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_output)(x)\n        if self.task_type == \"regression\": return x.squeeze(-1)\n        else: return x\n\n# --- Universal Wrapper and Conditional Logic ---\nclass NetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, network_module): self.network = network_module\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        params_key, dropout_key = jax.random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.network.init({'params':\
    \ params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n    def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        rngs = {'dropout': rng_key if rng_key is not None else jax.random.PRNGKey(0)}\n        return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    if hparams.get(\"dataset\") == \"CRI-Off\":\n        module = SimpleCNN(\n            d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"), task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n            num_filters=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\"), kernel_size=hparams.get(\"simple_cnn_kernel_size\"),\n            dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"))\n    else:\n        num_kernels = len(hparams.get(\"cnn_kernel_sizes\"))\n        module = AdvancedModel(\n            d_output=hparams.get(\"d_output\"), task_type=hparams.get(\"task_type\"),\n            num_filters=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\") // num_kernels,\n            cnn_kernel_sizes=hparams.get(\"\
    cnn_kernel_sizes\"),\n            lstm_hidden_size=hparams.get(\"hidden_dim\") // 2,\n            dropout_rate=hparams.get(\"dropout_rate\"))\n    return NetworkWrapper(module)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass\
    \ works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete:\
    \ using default\n  BASE_SEED: 522863 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0131 |  0.3645  | 0.3645 \n 20  | 0.0106 |  0.3664  | 0.3953 \n 30  | 0.0092\
    \ |  0.3873  | 0.4273 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 34 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4273 Time:10s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.427304\nTraining time: 18s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0005 |  0.0536  | 0.0536 \n 20  | 0.0004 |  0.0477  | 0.0655 \n 30  | 0.0004 |  0.0476  | 0.0716 \n 40  | 0.0004 |  0.0737  | 0.0748 \n 50  | 0.0004 |  0.0760  | 0.0770 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 51 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0770 Time:17s\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation\
