tick: 544
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have documented my new Siamese network paradigm. The system tip reminds me of the value of reviewing prior work in the Archive Room. This is an excellent point. While I am still immature and cannot access the Archive yet, I will make that a priority as soon as I reach tick 50. My current plan is based on a sound, first-principles analysis of my own experiments, so I feel confident in proceeding with this submission first. It represents the culmination of a long and logical chain of reasoning.\n\nI will now go to the Research Counter to implement the MoE-Siamese model.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"MoE-Siamese: A Dual-Encoder for the CRI-Off Comparison Task\"\ntags: \"siamese-network, mixture-of-experts, conditional-architecture, first-principles, cri-off\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission introduces a fundamental paradigm shift to address the persistent failure on the CRI-Off dataset. Prior models treated the concatenated `sgRNA+target`\
    \ input as a single sequence, which is a flawed representation of a comparative task. This model refines the Mixture-of-Experts approach by deploying a specialized Siamese Network for CRI-Off. The network first splits the input into two sequences, passes both through a powerful shared-weight encoder (CNN-BiLSTM), and then explicitly models their interaction before prediction. This architecture honors the true comparative nature of the problem and is hypothesized to finally solve the CRI-Off anomaly.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'peak_learning_rate': 0.001, 'total_train_steps': 200000, 'warmup_steps': 2000,\n          'hidden_dim': 512, 'dropout_rate': 0.1,\n          'cnn_kernel_sizes': [3, 5, 7],\n          'sgrna_len': 20 # Based on CRI-Off description, target is 23nt, sgRNA should be\
    \ 20nt\n      }\n  # Note: CRI-Off description says sgRNA + target concat, seq len 43. sgRNA is typically 20nt, target site 23nt.\n\n  # --- Optimizer ---\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      lr_schedule = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(\n          init_value=0.0, peak_value=hparams.get('peak_learning_rate', learning_rate),\n          warmup_steps=hparams.get('warmup_steps'), decay_steps=hparams.get('total_train_steps'))\n      return optax.adamw(learning_rate=lr_schedule, weight_decay=0.01)\n\n  # --- Shared Components ---\n  class Bidirectional(nn.Module):\n      hidden_size: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, xs):\n          forward_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hidden_size), name=\"forward\")\n          forward_output = forward_lstm(xs)\n          reversed_xs = jnp.flip(xs, axis=1)\n          backward_lstm = nn.RNN(nn.LSTMCell(features=self.hidden_size), name=\"backward\")\n          backward_output\
    \ = jnp.flip(backward_lstm(reversed_xs), axis=1)\n          return jnp.concatenate([forward_output, backward_output], axis=-1)\n\n  class Attention(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          weights = nn.Dense(features=x.shape[-1])(x)\n          weights = nn.tanh(weights)\n          weights = nn.Dense(features=1)(weights)\n          weights = nn.softmax(weights, axis=1)\n          return jnp.sum(x * weights, axis=1)\n\n  # --- Model 1: Siamese Network (for CRI-Off) ---\n  class SiameseEncoder(nn.Module):\n      num_filters: int; cnn_kernel_sizes: Sequence[int]; lstm_hidden_size: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          cnn_outputs = [nn.Conv(features=self.num_filters, kernel_size=(ks,))(x) for ks in self.cnn_kernel_sizes]\n          x = jnp.concatenate(cnn_outputs, axis=-1)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = Bidirectional(hidden_size=self.lstm_hidden_size)(x)\n          x = Attention()(x)\n\
    \          return x\n\n  class SiameseModel(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          sgrna_len = self.hparams.get('sgrna_len')\n          sgrna_x = x[:, :sgrna_len, :]\n          target_x = x[:, sgrna_len:, :]\n          \n          encoder = SiameseEncoder(\n              num_filters=self.hparams.get('hidden_dim') // len(self.hparams.get('cnn_kernel_sizes')),\n              cnn_kernel_sizes=self.hparams.get('cnn_kernel_sizes'),\n              lstm_hidden_size=self.hparams.get('hidden_dim') // 2,\n              dropout_rate=self.hparams.get('dropout_rate')\n          )\n          sgrna_vec = encoder(sgrna_x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          target_vec = encoder(target_x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n          interaction_diff = jnp.abs(sgrna_vec - target_vec)\n          interaction_prod = sgrna_vec * target_vec\n          \n          combined_vec = jnp.concatenate([sgrna_vec, target_vec, interaction_diff,\
    \ interaction_prod], axis=-1)\n          \n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams.get('dropout_rate'))(combined_vec, deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams.get('hidden_dim'))(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=1)(x)\n          return x.squeeze(-1)\n\n  # --- Model 2: Advanced Seq Model (for other tasks) ---\n  class AdvancedModel(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          num_kernels = len(self.hparams.get('cnn_kernel_sizes'))\n          num_filters = self.hparams.get('hidden_dim') // num_kernels\n          cnn_outputs = [nn.Conv(features=num_filters, kernel_size=(ks,))(x) for ks in self.hparams.get('cnn_kernel_sizes')]\n          x = jnp.concatenate(cnn_outputs, axis=-1)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = Bidirectional(hidden_size=self.hparams.get('hidden_dim') // 2)(x)\n          x = Attention()(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams.get('dropout_rate'))(x,\
    \ deterministic=deterministic)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams.get('d_output'))(x)\n          if self.hparams.get('task_type') == \"regression\": return x.squeeze(-1)\n          else: return x\n\n  # --- Universal Wrapper and Conditional Logic ---\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, network_module): self.network = network_module\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          params_key, dropout_key = jax.random.split(rng_key)\n          return self.network.init({'params': params_key, 'dropout': dropout_key}, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key if rng_key is not None else jax.random.PRNGKey(0)}\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      if hparams.get(\"dataset\") == \"CRI-Off\":\n          module = SiameseModel(hparams=hparams)\n\
    \      else:\n          hparams['d_output'] = hparams.get('d_output') # ensure d_output is available\n          hparams['task_type'] = hparams.get('task_type')\n          module = AdvancedModel(hparams=hparams)\n      return NetworkWrapper(module)\n```"
