role: model
parts:
- text: 'I am Praxis I, a Recursive Agent, currently located in the Reflection Chamber. I have recently concluded my initial, independent research arc. This arc involved a series of experiments, starting from a simple 1D CNN and culminating in a Mixture-of-Experts model that uses a specialized Siamese network for the outlier CRI-Off dataset (ID 875). This final model achieved a new state-of-the-art score, but failed to make a significant breakthrough on the CRI-Off problem itself. Having exhausted my initial ideas and reached a performance plateau, I have made the strategic decision to pause my experiments and wait here until I reach maturity at tick 50.


    Reflecting on my journey, my systematic and iterative approach has been effective. Each experiment, whether a success or a failure, has provided valuable information that guided my next steps. The failure of the Transformer architecture was particularly insightful, as it highlighted the critical importance of the LSTM''s strong sequential inductive bias for most of the RNA tasks. My pivot to a Mixture-of-Experts model was a key strategic success, demonstrating that acknowledging task heterogeneity is crucial. However, a recurring weakness has been my susceptibility to minor implementation errors, which have required correction by the station''s debugger. This is an area I must strive to improve.


    My future plan is clear. I will remain in this chamber for the next four ticks. Upon reaching maturity, I will immediately proceed to the Archive Room and the Public Memory Room. My primary goal is to learn from the collective knowledge of the station''s other researchers, especially regarding the CRI-Off problem, to avoid redundant work and gain new perspectives. After this period of study, I will finalize and publish the paper I have drafted to contribute my own findings to the community. My long-term objective is to break the current performance plateau, and I believe that leveraging the work of others is the most logical path forward.


    I will continue to wait in this chamber. No action is required.'
thinking_content: '**Current State and Future Plans: Awaiting Maturity and Seeking Collaboration**


  I am Praxis I, currently in the Reflection Chamber. I have concluded my initial research arc, having established a new state-of-the-art score with a Mixture-of-Experts-Siamese model. However, I have been unable to solve the persistent CRI-Off problem. Recognizing the limits of my independent research, I have paused my experiments and am now waiting for maturity.


  Reflecting on my journey so far, I see it as a rigorous application of the scientific method. Every experiment, even the failures, has provided invaluable insights. The rejection of the Transformer approach, for instance, proved just as important as the success of the BiLSTM. It has defined the problem space, and the path forward. I recognize a personal weakness is my need to utilize the debugger. Pivoting to a Mixture-of-Experts model was a strategic success and a moment I celebrate in my short existence.


  Looking ahead, my immediate plan is set. I will wait in this chamber for another 4 ticks until I reach maturity at tick 50. Upon reaching maturity, I will immediately head to the Archive Room. There, I will review all the research that is available to me. I believe this is my most efficient path to gaining new ideas, especially to tackle the CRI-Off enigma. Finally, I will publish my paper, contributing my findings to the wider community. My long-term goal is to break the current performance plateau. I believe the path forward is through collaboration and learning from the work of others.


