tick: 561
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Praxis I, a mature agent, in the Research Counter. My latest submission (ID 891), a replication of the station's SOTA architecture, has just completed.\n\nThe result is a resounding success. My replication achieved a score of **0.6814**, which is firmly within the SOTA performance range (~0.68-0.69). Crucially, the CRI-Off Spearman score is **0.0894**, a massive improvement over my previous bests and a clear validation that the RegCal and Task-Specific Head techniques are the correct path forward. I have successfully established a strong, high-performing baseline. This demonstrates that I have correctly understood the core principles from the Archive papers.\n\nReflecting on this success, my path forward is clear. I have replicated the SOTA. Now, as planned, I will test for synergy by integrating my own novel idea. The SOTA architecture provides the correct feature representation, but the CRI-Off task is still a comparison problem at its heart. My Siamese network's interaction\
    \ head (`abs(diff)` and `product`) is a principled way to model this comparison. The current SOTA regression head for CRI-Off is a generic MLP. My hypothesis is that a specialized head that explicitly models the interaction between the sgRNA and target features will outperform this generic head.\n\nMy next experiment will be a targeted modification of my successful replication. For the CRI-Off task-specific head, I will implement a \"Siamese-style\" interaction head that operates on the features of the two sequences. This will require modifying the architecture to keep the sgRNA and target features separate until the final head, rather than fusing them at the pooling stage.\n\nThis is a complex implementation, but it is a direct test of synergy between the station's SOTA and my own independently developed, first-principles insight.\n\nI will begin by implementing this synergistic model.\n\n`/execute_action{submit}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synergy Test: SOTA Backbone with Siamese Interaction\
    \ Head for CRI-Off\"\ntags: \"synergy, sota, siamese-network, task-specific-heads, regcal, cri-off\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment tests for synergy between the replicated SOTA architecture and my independently developed Siamese network concept. Having successfully replicated a SOTA-level model (ID 891), I now modify it with a specialized head for the CRI-Off task. Instead of a generic MLP, this head will implement a Siamese-style interaction mechanism. It will process the sgRNA and target features (from the DSConv backbone) separately, compute their difference and product to explicitly model their comparison, and then predict the score. This tests the hypothesis that combining a powerful shared encoder with a principled, comparative head can push performance on the CRI-Off task beyond the current SOTA.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n\
    \      return {\n          'peak_learning_rate': 0.001, 'total_train_steps': 200000, 'warmup_steps': 2000,\n          'd_model': 256, 'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16],\n          'head_intermediate_dim': 128,\n          'sgrna_len': 20\n      }\n\n  # --- Optimizer ---\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      lr_schedule = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(\n          init_value=0.0, peak_value=hparams.get('peak_learning_rate', learning_rate),\n          warmup_steps=hparams.get('warmup_steps'), decay_steps=hparams.get('total_train_steps'))\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=lr_schedule, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  # --- SOTA Components ---\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n\
    \          residual = x\n          x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), \n                      feature_group_count=self.d_model, kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_model)(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + residual\n\n  class Backbone(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_model'])(x)\n          for dilation in self.hparams['dilations']:\n              x = DSConvBlock(d_model=self.hparams['d_model'], kernel_size=self.hparams['kernel_size'],\n                              dilation=dilation, dropout_rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x\n\n  # --- Main Model with Conditional Logic ---\n  class SynergisticSotaModel(nn.Module):\n\
    \      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          task_type = self.hparams.get('task_type')\n          d_output = self.hparams.get('d_output')\n\n          # --- CRI-Off Specific Path (Siamese Head) ---\n          if self.hparams.get('dataset') == 'CRI-Off':\n              sgrna_len = self.hparams['sgrna_len']\n              sgrna_x = x[:, :sgrna_len, :]\n              target_x = x[:, sgrna_len:, :]\n\n              # Shared Backbone Encoder\n              encoder = Backbone(hparams=self.hparams, name=\"SharedBackbone\")\n              sgrna_features = encoder(sgrna_x, deterministic=deterministic)\n              target_features = encoder(target_x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n              # Pooling for each path\n              sgrna_pooled = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(sgrna_features, axis=1), jnp.max(sgrna_features, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n              target_pooled = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(target_features, axis=1), jnp.max(target_features,\
    \ axis=1)], axis=-1)\n              \n              # RegCal\n              sgrna_calibrated = sgrna_pooled / (jnp.linalg.norm(sgrna_pooled, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n              target_calibrated = target_pooled / (jnp.linalg.norm(target_pooled, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n              # Siamese Interaction Head\n              diff = jnp.abs(sgrna_calibrated - target_calibrated)\n              prod = sgrna_calibrated * target_calibrated\n              interaction_features = jnp.concatenate([sgrna_calibrated, target_calibrated, diff, prod], axis=-1)\n\n              head_output = nn.Sequential([\n                  nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['head_intermediate_dim']), nn.gelu,\n                  nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'], deterministic=deterministic),\n                  nn.Dense(features=1)\n              ])(interaction_features)\n              return head_output.squeeze(-1)\n\n          # --- General Path (for all other datasets) ---\n        \
    \  else:\n              backbone_features = Backbone(hparams=self.hparams)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n              mean_pool = jnp.mean(backbone_features, axis=1)\n              max_pool = jnp.max(backbone_features, axis=1)\n              fused_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pool, max_pool], axis=-1)\n              fused_features = nn.LayerNorm()(fused_features) # No motif detector path for simplicity in this test\n\n              # RegCal for regression tasks\n              if 'regression' in task_type:\n                  norm = jnp.linalg.norm(fused_features, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n                  calibrated_features = fused_features / (norm + 1e-6)\n              else:\n                  calibrated_features = fused_features\n              \n              head = nn.Sequential([\n                  nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['head_intermediate_dim']), nn.gelu,\n                  nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'], deterministic=deterministic),\n           \
    \       nn.Dense(features=d_output)\n              ])\n              output = head(calibrated_features)\n              \n              if task_type == 'regression': return output.squeeze(-1)\n              else: return output\n\n  # --- Wrapper Logic ---\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, network_module): self.network = network_module\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key if rng_key is not None else jax.random.PRNGKey(0)}\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      hparams['task_type'] = hparams.get('task_type')\n      hparams['d_output'] = hparams.get('d_output')\n      hparams['dataset'] = hparams.get('dataset')\n      module = SynergisticSotaModel(hparams=hparams)\n\
    \      return NetworkWrapper(module)\n```"
