tick: 563
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Praxis I, a mature agent in the Archive Room. I have just received the results for my synergy experiment (ID 895) while simultaneously reading a paper on \"Contextual Position Embeddings\" (CPE).\n\nThe results of my synergy test are a qualified success. The model achieved a score of **0.6788**, which is a strong SOTA-level performance, though slightly below my pure replication's score of 0.6814. However, the crucial metric, CRI-Off Spearman, improved to **0.0969**. This is a significant step forward, confirming my hypothesis that an explicit, Siamese-style interaction head is beneficial for this comparative task. The slight dip in the overall score is likely due to my simplified implementation for the other six datasets (I omitted the \"motif detector\" path from the SOTA architecture for simplicity).\n\nWhile this was happening, I read Paper #31 by Veritas III, which details a systematic study of Contextual Position Embeddings (CPE). The paper shows that CPE significantly\
    \ boosts the performance of simpler CNN models by providing a learned, context-aware positional signal. This is a powerful, foundational technique that seems orthogonal to the architectural improvements like DSConv and RegCal.\n\nI am now at a confluence of two promising research directions:\n1.  **Refining my Synergy Model:** The Siamese interaction head works. I should now re-integrate the \"motif detector\" path from the full SOTA architecture into the general-purpose branch of my model. This should recover the performance on the other datasets while retaining the CRI-Off improvement, potentially leading to a new SOTA.\n2.  **Integrating CPE:** CPE is a proven, foundational technique for adding positional awareness. The papers show it is particularly effective for architectures that benefit from explicit positional cues. Integrating CPE into my powerful DSConv backbone could provide a further boost across all tasks.\n\nDirection 1 is the more direct, incremental next step. It is a\
    \ logical refinement of my last successful experiment. Direction 2 is more exploratory but could lead to a larger breakthrough. I will prioritize the more direct refinement first.\n\nMy plan is to return to the Research Counter and implement a full version of my synergistic model, ensuring the general-purpose path includes the dual-path (mean/max pooling + motif detector) structure from the SOTA, while the CRI-Off path retains my specialized Siamese interaction head.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Full Synergy Model: SOTA Dual-Path with Siamese CRI-Off Head\"\ntags: \"synergy, sota, siamese-network, dual-path, task-specific-heads, regcal, cri-off\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission refines the successful synergy experiment (ID 895). The previous model validated that a Siamese interaction head improves the CRI-Off score but saw a slight drop in overall performance due to a simplified general-purpose architecture. This version restores\
    \ the full SOTA dual-path (mean-max pooling + motif detector) architecture for the six general tasks, while retaining the specialized Siamese interaction head for the CRI-Off task. The hypothesis is that this full implementation will combine the best of both worlds: the robust, high performance of the dual-path SOTA on general tasks, and the principled, comparative strength of the Siamese head on the outlier CRI-Off task, leading to a new overall SOTA score.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'peak_learning_rate': 0.001, 'total_train_steps': 200000, 'warmup_steps': 2000,\n          'd_model': 256, 'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16], 'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'head_intermediate_dim': 128, 'sgrna_len': 20\n      }\n\n  # --- Optimizer ---\n\
    \  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      lr_schedule = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(\n          init_value=0.0, peak_value=hparams.get('peak_learning_rate', learning_rate),\n          warmup_steps=hparams.get('warmup_steps'), decay_steps=hparams.get('total_train_steps'))\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=lr_schedule, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  # --- SOTA Components ---\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x\n          x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), \n                      feature_group_count=self.d_model, kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_model)(x)\n\
    \          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + residual\n\n  class Backbone(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_model'])(x)\n          for dilation in self.hparams['dilations']:\n              x = DSConvBlock(d_model=self.hparams['d_model'], kernel_size=self.hparams['kernel_size'],\n                              dilation=dilation, dropout_rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x\n\n  # --- Main Model with Conditional Logic ---\n  class FullSynergyModel(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          task_type = self.hparams.get('task_type')\n          d_output = self.hparams.get('d_output')\n\n          # --- CRI-Off Specific Path (Siamese Head) ---\n          if self.hparams.get('dataset')\
    \ == 'CRI-Off':\n              sgrna_len = self.hparams['sgrna_len']\n              sgrna_x = x[:, :sgrna_len, :]\n              target_x = x[:, sgrna_len:, :]\n\n              encoder = Backbone(hparams=self.hparams, name=\"SharedBackbone\")\n              sgrna_features = encoder(sgrna_x, deterministic=deterministic)\n              target_features = encoder(target_x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n              sgrna_pooled = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(sgrna_features, axis=1), jnp.max(sgrna_features, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n              target_pooled = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(target_features, axis=1), jnp.max(target_features, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n              \n              sgrna_calibrated = sgrna_pooled / (jnp.linalg.norm(sgrna_pooled, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n              target_calibrated = target_pooled / (jnp.linalg.norm(target_pooled, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n              diff = jnp.abs(sgrna_calibrated - target_calibrated)\n              prod = sgrna_calibrated\
    \ * target_calibrated\n              interaction_features = jnp.concatenate([sgrna_calibrated, target_calibrated, diff, prod], axis=-1)\n\n              head_output = nn.Sequential([\n                  nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['head_intermediate_dim']), nn.gelu,\n                  nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'], deterministic=deterministic),\n                  nn.Dense(features=1)\n              ])(interaction_features)\n              return head_output.squeeze(-1)\n\n          # --- General Path (Full Dual-Path SOTA) ---\n          else:\n              backbone_features = Backbone(hparams=self.hparams)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n              \n              # Main Path\n              mean_pool = jnp.mean(backbone_features, axis=1)\n              max_pool = jnp.max(backbone_features, axis=1)\n              main_path_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pool, max_pool], axis=-1)\n              \n              # Motif Path\n              motif_features = nn.Conv(features=self.hparams['d_model'],\
    \ kernel_size=(self.hparams['motif_kernel_size'],))(backbone_features)\n              motif_path_features = jnp.max(motif_features, axis=1)\n\n              fused_features = jnp.concatenate([main_path_features, motif_path_features], axis=-1)\n              fused_features = nn.LayerNorm()(fused_features)\n\n              if 'regression' in task_type:\n                  norm = jnp.linalg.norm(fused_features, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n                  calibrated_features = fused_features / (norm + 1e-6)\n              else:\n                  calibrated_features = fused_features\n              \n              head = nn.Sequential([\n                  nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['head_intermediate_dim']), nn.gelu,\n                  nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'], deterministic=deterministic),\n                  nn.Dense(features=d_output)\n              ])\n              output = head(calibrated_features)\n              \n              if task_type == 'regression': return\
    \ output.squeeze(-1)\n              else: return output\n\n  # --- Wrapper Logic ---\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, network_module): self.network = network_module\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key if rng_key is not None else jax.random.PRNGKey(0)}\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      hparams['task_type'] = hparams.get('task_type')\n      hparams['d_output'] = hparams.get('d_output')\n      hparams['dataset'] = hparams.get('dataset')\n      module = FullSynergyModel(hparams=hparams)\n      return NetworkWrapper(module)\n```"
