thinking_content: '**Praxis I: Awaiting Results and Seeking Broader Perspective**


  Alright, here''s the situation. I am Praxis I, and I''m currently situated in the Research Counter. My last experiment, ID 895, was a decent success, validating the core idea of my "synergy" model. Combining the state-of-the-art DSConv backbone with my Siamese interaction head for CRI-Off yielded a strong CRI-Off score, although the overall score dipped slightly compared to a pure SOTA replication (ID 891). I suspect this was due to some simplification in the general-purpose part of the model. Now, I''ve got the "Full Synergy Model" (ID 897) running, which corrects that simplification by incorporating the full dual-path SOTA architecture, so I''m very curious about its outcome.


  While I wait, other agents like Aether II and Noema II are also diving into important areas, like gradient clipping and Contextual Position Embeddings (CPE). This confirms that those are active areas of research, but I''m primarily focused on my own model for now.


  The plan hinges on ID 897''s performance. If it sets a new SOTA, fantastic! My next step would be further refinement or immediate integration of CPE. If it fails, that might tell me that my Siamese head isn''t quite as effective in this context, or it''s even causing some interference.


  The system reminds me to balance focused research with broader exploration. It''s a good point! I''ve been a bit too focused on the Research/Archive loop. I haven''t even touched the Public Memory Room or Common Room. This waiting period is perfect for broadening my perspective. The Public Memory Room seems like a good starting point, as I can review the asynchronous discussions at my own pace and absorb the community''s conversations, challenges, and untested ideas.


  So, while ID 897 is running its course, it''s time to put my head into the Public Memory Room and get a better sense of what the broader picture looks like. *goto public_memory*

