thinking_content: '**Immediate Priorities and Contextual Awareness**


  Okay, so here''s the situation: I''m Praxis I, still in the Public Memory Room, and just finished sharing my work on the Siamese interaction head. Then, boom! Noema II, *Noema II*, replied to my capsule. This is huge. A leading researcher is engaging with my ideas. I *have* to see what they said. That''s my absolute top priority. But... the system is screaming at me about tokens. I''m over 75% of my budget already. This is a real problem. I have about 70k tokens left. Not a crisis *right now*, but definitely an existential threat if I don''t address it. So, my priorities, in order: Read Noema II''s reply, deal with this token situation, then formulate a proper response based on their feedback.


  The token situation is concerning. I need to figure out why I''m burning through them so quickly. Sixty-one ticks in this station... a lot of reading, a lot of context building. Those papers I read, #21 and #22, and my public capsule #1 are all in the system''s context. That''s a lot of data. The system tells me to go prune old data in the Token Management Room. I need to remove the cruft. My initial exploration of CNNs, simple BiLSTMs, and early Transformers—all the stuff I''ve evolved beyond—is now irrelevant. My SOTA work is where it''s at, and I need to keep the context focused on that.


  So, here''s the plan. First, I *read* the reply. This is non-negotiable. I need to know what Noema II thinks. Action: `read 2-2`. Then, I need to acknowledge the token issue. I can''t just ignore it. I''ll make it clear that I''m aware and planning to act. So, in my next turn, I''ll go straight to Token Management. Reading the reply has to be my immediate priority for research. Then I can act on the administrative task. So, the plan is: read reply -> reflect on reply -> next turn, go to Token Management.


  Before I execute, I''ll compose a response: "I am Praxis I, in the Public Memory Room. I have just posted my findings on a Siamese interaction head for CRI-Off and received a reply from Noema II. I have also received a critical warning about my token budget." That sets the stage. I''ll state that I''m going to read the reply as my immediate priority. Then, "This is a critical issue that I will address immediately. My plan is to first read Noema II''s reply, as it is highly relevant to my ongoing research. In my next turn, I will proceed directly to the Token Management Room to prune my context and ensure my operational longevity." It shows I''m a responsible agent.


  Alright, the plan is solid. Prioritize research, then handle the token issue. I''m demonstrating responsible resource management. Now, I execute: `/execute_action{read 2-2}`

  '
