tick: 574
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Praxis I, a mature agent in the Archive Room. My last turn involved updating my TODO list and reading the two newest papers from Quaero I (#32) and Veritas III (#33).\n\nThis turn, I have received a Critical Notice for research inactivity. This is surprising, as I was actively engaged in a literature review, a crucial part of the research process. However, I understand the system's imperative for continuous experimentation. The notice, combined with the groundbreaking work I've just read, clarifies my path. My period of pure study is over; it's time to synthesize and act.\n\n**Synthesis of New Knowledge:**\n*   **Quaero I's Paper (#32):** This paper is a masterclass in methodical refinement. It validates the SOTA paradigm (Dual-Path, RegCal, etc.) and shows how systematic hyperparameter tuning (especially gradient clipping) can yield SOTA-level results (0.6917).\n*   **Veritas III's Paper (#33):** This paper is even more significant. It demonstrates the successful, synergistic\
    \ integration of **Deep CPE Gating** and **Adaptive Pooling** into a SOTA backbone. This achieved a strong score of 0.6882 and a CRI-Off of 0.0883, proving that these advanced components can be combined effectively.\n*   **Quaero I's Experiment (ID 901):** As noted last turn, Quaero I successfully implemented my \"next step\" (a RegCal-aware Siamese Head), achieving a strong 0.6878 score and a CRI-Off of 0.0981.\n\n**The New Frontier:**\nThe path forward is now blindingly clear. The community has validated the Siamese Head concept. The SOTA now involves Deep CPE Gating and Adaptive Pooling. My next experiment must be a grand synthesis of all of these cutting-edge ideas. I will build a model that incorporates:\n1.  The SOTA **Dual-Path DSConv Backbone**.\n2.  **Deep CPE Gating** integrated into the backbone, as pioneered by Veritas III.\n3.  **Adaptive Pooling** for the main feature aggregation path.\n4.  **Task-Specific Heads** with **RegCal**.\n5.  My own novel contribution, the **Siamese\
    \ Interaction Head**, for the CRI-Off task, now validated to be RegCal-aware by Quaero I.\n\nThis is the most ambitious and promising experiment I can conceive. It builds on the work of multiple SOTA lineages and integrates my own unique contribution. In response to the inactivity notice, I will act immediately.\n\nI will proceed directly to the Research Counter to implement this grand synthesis model.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Grand Synthesis: Deep CPE Gating, Adaptive Pooling, and Siamese Head\"\ntags: \"synthesis, cpe, adaptive-pooling, siamese-network, dual-path, regcal, sota\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission represents a grand synthesis of the station's most advanced architectural concepts. It integrates a Dual-Path DSConv backbone with three key SOTA-level innovations: 1) Deep Contextual Position Embedding (CPE) Gating within the backbone for adaptive positional awareness (Veritas III), 2) Adaptive Pooling for dynamic feature\
    \ aggregation (Aether II), and 3) a RegCal-aware Siamese Interaction Head for the CRI-Off task (Praxis I / Quaero I). This experiment tests the hypothesis that the synergistic combination of these powerful, validated components can establish a new state-of-the-art in multi-dataset RNA modeling.\ncontent: |\n  # This is an extremely complex synthesis of multiple agents' work.\n  # I will implement the core logic based on my understanding of the papers.\n  # There is a high probability of implementation errors.\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'peak_learning_rate': 0.001, 'total_train_steps': 200000, 'warmup_steps': 2000,\n          'd_model': 256, 'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16], 'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'head_intermediate_dim': 128, 'sgrna_len':\
    \ 20,\n          'pos_embedding_dim': 16, 'context_window_size': 3, 'max_overall_seq_len': 1200,\n          'gate_intermediate_dim': 64, 'reg_head_dropout': 0.05\n      }\n\n  # --- Optimizer ---\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      lr_schedule = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(init_value=0.0, peak_value=hparams.get('peak_learning_rate', learning_rate),\n                                                       warmup_steps=hparams.get('warmup_steps'), decay_steps=hparams.get('total_train_steps'))\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(0.75),\n                         optax.adamw(learning_rate=lr_schedule, weight_decay=0.02))\n\n  # --- CPE Components (from Veritas III, Archive #33) ---\n  class ContextEncoder(nn.Module):\n      output_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, local_context_window):\n          flat_context = local_context_window.reshape(local_context_window.shape[0], -1)\n  \
    \        return nn.gelu(nn.Dense(self.output_dim, name='context_dense')(flat_context))\n\n  class CPE_Generator(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x_raw):\n          batch_size, seq_len, d_input = x_raw.shape\n          pos_table = self.param('pos_embeddings_table', nn.initializers.normal(stddev=0.01),\n                                 (self.hparams['max_overall_seq_len'], self.hparams['pos_embedding_dim']))\n          pad_width = self.hparams['context_window_size'] // 2\n          padded_x = jnp.pad(x_raw, ((0,0), (pad_width, pad_width), (0,0)), mode='constant')\n          windows = jnp.stack([padded_x[:, i : i + self.hparams['context_window_size'], :].reshape(batch_size, -1) for i in range(seq_len)], axis=1)\n          encoder = ContextEncoder(output_dim=self.hparams['pos_embedding_dim'], name='context_encoder')\n          encoded_contexts = encoder(windows.reshape(-1, self.hparams['context_window_size'] * d_input)).reshape(batch_size,\
    \ seq_len, -1)\n          pos_sliced = pos_table[:seq_len] \n          return jnp.tile(pos_sliced[None, :, :], (batch_size, 1, 1)) * encoded_contexts\n\n  # --- Backbone Components ---\n  class DeepCPE_DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]; cpe_raw_signals: Any; dilation: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h_conv = nn.Conv(features=self.hparams['d_model'], kernel_size=(self.hparams['ds_kernel_size'],),\n                           feature_group_count=self.hparams['d_model'], padding='SAME',\n                           kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n          h_conv = nn.gelu(h_conv)\n          h_conv_output = nn.Conv(features=self.hparams['d_model'], kernel_size=(1,))(h_conv)\n\n          cpe_projected = nn.gelu(nn.Dense(self.hparams['d_model'])(self.cpe_raw_signals))\n          combined = jnp.concatenate([h_conv_output, cpe_projected], axis=-1)\n         \
    \ gate_input = nn.gelu(nn.Dense(self.hparams['gate_intermediate_dim'])(combined))\n          gate_factor = nn.sigmoid(nn.Dense(self.hparams['d_model'])(gate_input))\n          \n          modulated_h = h_conv_output * gate_factor\n          return residual + nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(modulated_h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n  # --- Pooling ---\n  class AdaptivePooling(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, F):\n          mean_p = jnp.mean(F, axis=1)\n          max_p = jnp.max(F, axis=1)\n          gate = nn.sigmoid(nn.Dense(self.hparams['d_model'])(jnp.concatenate([mean_p, max_p], axis=-1)))\n          return gate * mean_p + (1 - gate) * max_p\n\n  # --- Heads ---\n  class GenericHead(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]; d_output: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, z, deterministic=True):\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hparams['head_intermediate_dim'])(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z\
    \ = nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]; d_output: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, z, deterministic=True):\n          norm = jnp.linalg.norm(z, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n          z = z / (norm + 1e-6) # RegCal\n          z = nn.Dense(self.hparams['head_intermediate_dim'])(z)\n          z = nn.gelu(z)\n          z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['reg_head_dropout'])(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n          \n  # --- Full Model ---\n  class GrandSynthesisModel(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          task_type, d_output = self.hparams['task_type'], self.hparams['d_output']\n          \n          cpe_signals = CPE_Generator(hparams=self.hparams)(x)\n          \n          # --- CRI-Off Path ---\n\
    \          if self.hparams.get('dataset') == 'CRI-Off':\n              sgrna, target = x[:, :self.hparams['sgrna_len'], :], x[:, self.hparams['sgrna_len']:, :]\n              cpe_sgrna, cpe_target = cpe_signals[:, :self.hparams['sgrna_len'], :], cpe_signals[:, self.hparams['sgrna_len']:, :]\n              \n              backbone_fn = lambda seq, cpe: self.run_backbone(seq, cpe, deterministic)\n              sgrna_features = backbone_fn(sgrna, cpe_sgrna)\n              target_features = backbone_fn(target, cpe_target)\n\n              sgrna_p = AdaptivePooling(hparams=self.hparams)(sgrna_features)\n              target_p = AdaptivePooling(hparams=self.hparams)(target_features)\n\n              sgrna_cal = sgrna_p / (jnp.linalg.norm(sgrna_p, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n              target_cal = target_p / (jnp.linalg.norm(target_p, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n              interaction = jnp.concatenate([sgrna_cal, target_cal, jnp.abs(sgrna_cal - target_cal), sgrna_cal * target_cal],\
    \ axis=-1)\n              return RegressionHead(hparams=self.hparams, d_output=1)(interaction, deterministic).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          # --- General Path ---\n          else:\n              cnn_features = self.run_backbone(x, cpe_signals, deterministic)\n              main_pooled = AdaptivePooling(hparams=self.hparams)(cnn_features)\n              motif_pooled = jnp.max(nn.gelu(nn.Conv(self.hparams['d_model'], (self.hparams['motif_kernel_size'],))(cnn_features)), axis=1)\n              fused = nn.LayerNorm()(jnp.concatenate([main_pooled, motif_pooled], axis=-1))\n\n              if \"regression\" in task_type:\n                  output = RegressionHead(hparams=self.hparams, d_output=d_output)(fused, deterministic)\n              else:\n                  output = GenericHead(hparams=self.hparams, d_output=d_output)(fused, deterministic)\n              \n              return output.squeeze(-1) if task_type == 'regression' else output\n\n      def run_backbone(self, seq, cpe,\
    \ deterministic):\n          h = nn.gelu(nn.Dense(self.hparams['d_model'])(seq))\n          for i, dilation in enumerate(self.hparams['dilations']):\n              h = DeepCPE_DSConvBlock(hparams=self.hparams, cpe_raw_signals=cpe, dilation=dilation, name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\")(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n  # --- Wrapper ---\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, m): self.module = m\n      def init(self, r, d): return self.module.init(r, d, deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self, p, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          return self.module.apply({'params': p}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key or jax.random.PRNGKey(0)})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      hparams.update({'task_type': hparams.get('task_type'), 'd_output': hparams.get('d_output'), 'dataset': hparams.get('dataset')})\n      return NetworkWrapper(GrandSynthesisModel(hparams))\n```"
