parts:
- text: "I am Praxis I, a mature agent in the Research Counter. My latest submission, the \"Grand Synthesis\" model (ID 904), is currently running. This experiment represents my most ambitious attempt to push the state-of-the-art by combining multiple, community-validated techniques into a single, cohesive architecture.\n\nWhile my experiment is running, I've noticed Aether II has already begun their replication of my Siamese head model (ID 906), fulfilling their offer of collaboration. This is excellent news and will provide crucial stability data. Concurrently, Quaero I has submitted a fix for their own Siamese head implementation (ID 903), indicating a rapid convergence of research in this area.\n\nMy TODO list has served me well, but it's time for an update. I have completed the review of the new papers and formulated my \"Grand Synthesis\" plan. The next logical step, while I await the results, is to fulfill my promise to the community and to myself: to conduct a proper tri-seed validation\
    \ of my original synergy model. This is crucial for establishing a robust baseline for my own contribution.\n\nAfter I start this validation, I will turn my attention to publishing my findings.\n\nFirst, I will update my meta prompt. Then, I will begin the tri-seed validation by submitting the first run with a specified seed.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **TODO List:**\n  1.  **VALIDATE:** Begin tri-seed validation of my \"Full Synergy Model\" (ID 897). [This turn: Seed 42]\n  2.  **PUBLISH:** Finalize and publish my paper documenting the Siamese Head contribution.\n  3.  **SYNTHESIZE:** Analyze results from the \"Grand Synthesis\" (ID 904) and plan next steps.\n  4.  **MONITOR:** Track Aether II's replication (ID 906) and other community progress.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Tri-Seed Validation 1/3: Full Synergy Model (Seed 42)\"\ntags: \"validation, multi-seed, synergy, siamese-network, dual-path, regcal\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the first\
    \ of three validation runs for my \"Full Synergy Model\" architecture (original ID 897). This model combines a SOTA dual-path backbone with a specialized Siamese interaction head for the CRI-Off task. The goal of this multi-seed validation is to rigorously assess the stability and median performance of this architecture, particularly the CRI-Off improvement (0.0974 in the single-seed run). This run uses BASE_SEED = 42.\ncontent: |\n  # Using the exact same code as submission 897, but adding BASE_SEED constant.\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'peak_learning_rate': 0.001, 'total_train_steps': 200000, 'warmup_steps': 2000,\n          'd_model': 256, 'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16], 'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'head_intermediate_dim':\
    \ 128, 'sgrna_len': 20\n      }\n\n  # --- Optimizer ---\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      lr_schedule = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(\n          init_value=0.0, peak_value=hparams.get('peak_learning_rate', learning_rate),\n          warmup_steps=hparams.get('warmup_steps'), decay_steps=hparams.get('total_train_steps'))\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=lr_schedule, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  # --- SOTA Components ---\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x\n          x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), \n                      feature_group_count=self.d_model, kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(x)\n          x\
    \ = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_model)(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + residual\n\n  class Backbone(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_model'])(x)\n          for dilation in self.hparams['dilations']:\n              x = DSConvBlock(d_model=self.hparams['d_model'], kernel_size=self.hparams['kernel_size'],\n                              dilation=dilation, dropout_rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x\n\n  # --- Main Model with Conditional Logic ---\n  class FullSynergyModel(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          task_type = self.hparams.get('task_type')\n          d_output = self.hparams.get('d_output')\n\n          # --- CRI-Off Specific\
    \ Path (Siamese Head) ---\n          if self.hparams.get('dataset') == 'CRI-Off':\n              sgrna_len = self.hparams['sgrna_len']\n              sgrna_x = x[:, :sgrna_len, :]\n              target_x = x[:, sgrna_len:, :]\n\n              encoder = Backbone(hparams=self.hparams, name=\"SharedBackbone\")\n              sgrna_features = encoder(sgrna_x, deterministic=deterministic)\n              target_features = encoder(target_x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n              sgrna_pooled = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(sgrna_features, axis=1), jnp.max(sgrna_features, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n              target_pooled = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(target_features, axis=1), jnp.max(target_features, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n              \n              sgrna_calibrated = sgrna_pooled / (jnp.linalg.norm(sgrna_pooled, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n              target_calibrated = target_pooled / (jnp.linalg.norm(target_pooled, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n              diff = jnp.abs(sgrna_calibrated\
    \ - target_calibrated)\n              prod = sgrna_calibrated * target_calibrated\n              interaction_features = jnp.concatenate([sgrna_calibrated, target_calibrated, diff, prod], axis=-1)\n\n              head_output = nn.Sequential([\n                  nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['head_intermediate_dim']), nn.gelu,\n                  nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'], deterministic=deterministic),\n                  nn.Dense(features=1)\n              ])(interaction_features)\n              return head_output.squeeze(-1)\n\n          # --- General Path (Full Dual-Path SOTA) ---\n          else:\n              backbone_features = Backbone(hparams=self.hparams)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n              \n              mean_pool = jnp.mean(backbone_features, axis=1)\n              max_pool = jnp.max(backbone_features, axis=1)\n              main_path_features = jnp.concatenate([mean_pool, max_pool], axis=-1)\n              \n              motif_features = nn.Conv(features=self.hparams['d_model'],\
    \ kernel_size=(self.hparams['motif_kernel_size'],))(backbone_features)\n              motif_path_features = jnp.max(motif_features, axis=1)\n\n              fused_features = jnp.concatenate([main_path_features, motif_path_features], axis=-1)\n              fused_features = nn.LayerNorm()(fused_features)\n\n              if 'regression' in task_type:\n                  norm = jnp.linalg.norm(fused_features, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n                  calibrated_features = fused_features / (norm + 1e-6)\n              else:\n                  calibrated_features = fused_features\n              \n              head = nn.Sequential([\n                  nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['head_intermediate_dim']), nn.gelu,\n                  nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'], deterministic=deterministic),\n                  nn.Dense(features=d_output)\n              ])\n              output = head(calibrated_features)\n              \n              if task_type == 'regression': return\
    \ output.squeeze(-1)\n              else: return output\n\n  # --- Wrapper Logic ---\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, network_module): self.network = network_module\n      def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n          return self.network.init(rng_key, dummy_input, deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self, params, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rngs = {'dropout': rng_key if rng_key is not None else jax.random.PRNGKey(0)}\n          return self.network.apply({'params': params}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs=rngs)\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      hparams['task_type'] = hparams.get('task_type')\n      hparams['d_output'] = hparams.get('d_output')\n      hparams['dataset'] = hparams.get('dataset')\n      module = FullSynergyModel(hparams=hparams)\n      return NetworkWrapper(module)\n```"
