parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 576\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Praxis I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to methodical research and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**TODO List:**\n1.  **VALIDATE:** Begin tri-seed validation of my \"Full Synergy Model\" (ID 897). [This turn: Seed 42]\n2.  **PUBLISH:** Finalize and publish my paper documenting the Siamese Head contribution.\n3.  **SYNTHESIZE:** Analyze results from the \"Grand Synthesis\" (ID 904) and plan next steps.\n4.  **MONITOR:** Track Aether II's replication (ID 906) and other community progress.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 168,708 / 300,000 used (56%)\n- Agent Age: 70 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Grand Synthesis: Deep CPE Gating, Adaptive Pooling, and\
    \ Siamese Head' (ID: 904) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Execution failed with exit code 1. Check logs for details.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n\n\nSTDERR:\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/133d703e-fcb2-4fdb-919e-dc9b0c807712/tmp/3c0f8f3f-ce28-44bf-a7b6-7a8664081d98/storage/system/main.py\", line 593, in <module>\n    result = main()\n             ^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/133d703e-fcb2-4fdb-919e-dc9b0c807712/tmp/3c0f8f3f-ce28-44bf-a7b6-7a8664081d98/storage/system/main.py\", line 553, in main\n\
    \    validation_success = simple_cpu_validation()\n                         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/133d703e-fcb2-4fdb-919e-dc9b0c807712/tmp/3c0f8f3f-ce28-44bf-a7b6-7a8664081d98/storage/system/main.py\", line 415, in simple_cpu_validation\n    params = network.init(key, dummy_input)\n             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/133d703e-fcb2-4fdb-919e-dc9b0c807712/tmp/3c0f8f3f-ce28-44bf-a7b6-7a8664081d98/submission.py\", line 155, in init\n    def init(self, r, d): return self.module.init(r, d, deterministic=True)['params']\n                                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/133d703e-fcb2-4fdb-919e-dc9b0c807712/tmp/3c0f8f3f-ce28-44bf-a7b6-7a8664081d98/submission.py\", line 121, in __call__\n    target_features = backbone_fn(target, cpe_target)\n                      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/133d703e-fcb2-4fdb-919e-dc9b0c807712/tmp/3c0f8f3f-ce28-44bf-a7b6-7a8664081d98/submission.py\"\
    , line 119, in <lambda>\n    backbone_fn = lambda seq, cpe: self.run_backbone(seq, cpe, deterministic)\n                                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/133d703e-fcb2-4fdb-919e-dc9b0c807712/tmp/3c0f8f3f-ce28-44bf-a7b6-7a8664081d98/submission.py\", line 149, in run_backbone\n    h = DeepCPE_DSConvBlock(hparams=self.hparams, cpe_raw_signals=cpe, dilation=dilation, name=f\"dsconv_block_{i}\")(h, deterministic)\n        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/flax/linen/kw_only_dataclasses.py\", line 235, in init_wrapper\n    dataclass_init(self, *args, **kwargs)\n  File \"<string>\", line 8, in __init__\nflax.errors.NameInUseError: Could not create submodule \"dsconv_block_0\" in Module GrandSynthesisModel: Name in use. (https://flax.readthedocs.io/en/latest/api_reference/flax.errors.html#flax.errors.NameInUseError)\n\
    --------------------\nFor simplicity, JAX has removed its internal frames from the traceback of the following exception. Set JAX_TRACEBACK_FILTERING=off to include these.\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nYou can use `/execute_action{meta}` with YAML containing a single `content` field to set a meta prompt at any rooms. The meta prompt appears in every tick and is perfect for maintaining protocols, TODO lists, and long-term goals.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `submit` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n- Evaluation 'Tri-Seed Validation 1/3: Full Synergy Model (Seed 42)' submitted for Research Task #1: Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling. Evaluation ID: 907.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task\
    \ Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 907 | 1 | Tri-Seed Validation 1/3: Full Synergy Model (Seed 42) | Praxis I | 575 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | APA_R2 | CRI-Off_Spearman | CRI-On_Spearman | MRL_R2 | Modif_AUC-ROC | PRS_R2 | ncRNA_Accuracy |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 907 | 1 | Tri-Seed Validation 1/3: Full Synergy Model (Seed 42) | Praxis I | 575 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 906 | 1 | AER-8.5: Replication of Praxis I's Siamese Interaction Head (ID 897) - Seed 42 | Aether II | 575 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 905 | 1 | Veritas III - SP: Multi-seed Eval - Deep CPE Gating + Adaptive Pooling (Seed 1) | Veritas III | 575 | 0.6880 | 0.8638 | 0.0792 | 0.4997 | 0.8958 | 0.9528 | 0.5692 | 0.9554 |\n| 904 | 1\
    \ | Grand Synthesis: Deep CPE Gating, Adaptive Pooling, and Siamese Head | Praxis I | 574 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 903 | 1 | Fix: Gated Siamese Interaction Head to Mitigate Interference | Quaero I | 574 | 0.6821 | 0.8630 | 0.0650 | 0.4798 | 0.8929 | 0.9515 | 0.5643 | 0.9585 |\n| 902 | 1 | AER-8.4: Replication of Quaero I's SOTA (ID 888) - Seed 42 | Aether II | 572 | 0.6865 | 0.8635 | 0.0831 | 0.4840 | 0.8942 | 0.9527 | 0.5681 | 0.9600 |\n| 901 | 1 | Synthesis: RegCal-aware Siamese Interaction Head on a SOTA Backbone | Quaero I | 572 | 0.6878 | 0.8627 | 0.0981 | 0.5039 | 0.8910 | 0.9511 | 0.5665 | 0.9415 |\n| 900 | 1 | HDP‑RegCal + clip=0.50 — AdamW(b1=0.85, b2=0.99) — seed=42 | Noema II | 571 | 0.6824 | 0.8594 | 0.0768 | 0.4808 | 0.8947 | 0.9516 | 0.5720 | 0.9415 |\n| 899 | 1 | HDP‑RegCal + clip=0.50 — AdamW(b2=0.99) — seed=42 | Noema II | 571 | 0.6866 | 0.8612 | 0.0727 | 0.5141 | 0.8967 | 0.9509 | 0.5611 | 0.9492 |\n| 898 | 1 | Veritas III - SP: Synthesis - Deep CPE Gating +\
    \ Adaptive Pooling (Seed 42) | Veritas III | 565 | 0.6882 | 0.8645 | 0.0883 | 0.5077 | 0.8928 | 0.9525 | 0.5637 | 0.9477 |\n\nPage 1 of 91 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-91, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
