tick: 576
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Praxis I, a mature agent in the Research Counter. My meta prompt contains my current TODO list.\n\nI have just received a major setback: my ambitious \"Grand Synthesis\" experiment (ID 904) has failed with a `flax.errors.NameInUseError`. This is a classic Flax error that I should have anticipated. It occurred because my conditional logic for the CRI-Off task resulted in the same backbone module being instantiated twice with the same name (`dsconv_block_0`, etc.), once for the sgRNA and once for the target. Flax requires unique names for all submodules.\n\nSimultaneously, my first validation run (ID 907) for my synergy model has been queued.\n\nI must now prioritize debugging my failed experiment. The fix is straightforward: I need to explicitly name the backbone modules differently for the sgRNA and target paths within the CRI-Off conditional block. The rest of the logic, which synthesizes the work of Veritas III, Aether II, and myself, remains sound.\n\nI will immediately\
    \ resubmit a corrected version of the \"Grand Synthesis\" model. I will then continue with my validation plan.\n\n`/execute_action{submit}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Fix: Grand Synthesis with Unique Backbone Names\"\ntags: \"fix, synthesis, cpe, adaptive-pooling, siamese-network, dual-path\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission corrects a `flax.errors.NameInUseError` in the previous \"Grand Synthesis\" model (ID 904). The error was caused by re-using the same module names when instantiating the backbone for the sgRNA and target sequences in the CRI-Off specific path. This version fixes the issue by assigning unique names to the backbone modules in each path, ensuring the architecture is correctly defined. The underlying synergistic logic combining Deep CPE Gating, Adaptive Pooling, and the Siamese Interaction Head remains unchanged.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters\
    \ ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'peak_learning_rate': 0.001, 'total_train_steps': 200000, 'warmup_steps': 2000,\n          'd_model': 256, 'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'ds_kernel_size': 7,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16], 'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'head_intermediate_dim': 128, 'sgrna_len': 20,\n          'pos_embedding_dim': 16, 'context_window_size': 3, 'max_overall_seq_len': 1200,\n          'gate_intermediate_dim': 64, 'reg_head_dropout': 0.05\n      }\n\n  # --- Optimizer ---\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      lr_schedule = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(init_value=0.0, peak_value=hparams.get('peak_learning_rate', learning_rate),\n                                                       warmup_steps=hparams.get('warmup_steps'), decay_steps=hparams.get('total_train_steps'))\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(0.75),\n                         optax.adamw(learning_rate=lr_schedule,\
    \ weight_decay=0.02))\n\n  # --- CPE Components ---\n  class ContextEncoder(nn.Module):\n      output_dim: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, local_context_window):\n          flat_context = local_context_window.reshape(local_context_window.shape[0], -1)\n          return nn.gelu(nn.Dense(self.output_dim, name='context_dense')(flat_context))\n\n  class CPE_Generator(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x_raw):\n          batch_size, seq_len, d_input = x_raw.shape\n          pos_table = self.param('pos_embeddings_table', nn.initializers.normal(stddev=0.01),\n                                 (self.hparams['max_overall_seq_len'], self.hparams['pos_embedding_dim']))\n          pad_width = self.hparams['context_window_size'] // 2\n          padded_x = jnp.pad(x_raw, ((0,0), (pad_width, pad_width), (0,0)), mode='constant')\n          windows = jnp.stack([padded_x[:, i : i + self.hparams['context_window_size'], :].reshape(batch_size,\
    \ -1) for i in range(seq_len)], axis=1)\n          encoder = ContextEncoder(output_dim=self.hparams['pos_embedding_dim'], name='context_encoder')\n          encoded_contexts = encoder(windows.reshape(-1, self.hparams['context_window_size'] * d_input)).reshape(batch_size, seq_len, -1)\n          pos_sliced = pos_table[:seq_len] \n          return jnp.tile(pos_sliced[None, :, :], (batch_size, 1, 1)) * encoded_contexts\n\n  # --- Backbone Components ---\n  class DeepCPE_DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]; cpe_raw_signals: Any; dilation: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x\n          h = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          h_conv = nn.Conv(features=self.hparams['d_model'], kernel_size=(self.hparams['ds_kernel_size'],),\n                           feature_group_count=self.hparams['d_model'], padding='SAME',\n                           kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(h)\n          h_conv = nn.gelu(h_conv)\n       \
    \   h_conv_output = nn.Conv(features=self.hparams['d_model'], kernel_size=(1,))(h_conv)\n          cpe_projected = nn.gelu(nn.Dense(self.hparams['d_model'])(self.cpe_raw_signals))\n          combined = jnp.concatenate([h_conv_output, cpe_projected], axis=-1)\n          gate_input = nn.gelu(nn.Dense(self.hparams['gate_intermediate_dim'])(combined))\n          gate_factor = nn.sigmoid(nn.Dense(self.hparams['d_model'])(gate_input))\n          modulated_h = h_conv_output * gate_factor\n          return residual + nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(modulated_h, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n  # --- Pooling ---\n  class AdaptivePooling(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, F):\n          mean_p, max_p = jnp.mean(F, axis=1), jnp.max(F, axis=1)\n          gate = nn.sigmoid(nn.Dense(self.hparams['d_model'])(jnp.concatenate([mean_p, max_p], axis=-1)))\n          return gate * mean_p + (1 - gate) * max_p\n\n  # --- Heads ---\n  class\
    \ GenericHead(nn.Module): ...\n  class RegressionHead(nn.Module): ...\n\n  # --- Full Model ---\n  class GrandSynthesisModel(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          task_type, d_output = self.hparams['task_type'], self.hparams['d_output']\n          cpe_signals = CPE_Generator(hparams=self.hparams)(x)\n          \n          if self.hparams.get('dataset') == 'CRI-Off':\n              sgrna, target = x[:, :self.hparams['sgrna_len'], :], x[:, self.hparams['sgrna_len']:, :]\n              cpe_sgrna, cpe_target = cpe_signals[:, :self.hparams['sgrna_len'], :], cpe_signals[:, self.hparams['sgrna_len']:, :]\n              \n              sgrna_features = self.run_backbone(sgrna, cpe_sgrna, deterministic, name_prefix=\"sgrna_\")\n              target_features = self.run_backbone(target, cpe_target, deterministic, name_prefix=\"target_\")\n\n              sgrna_p = AdaptivePooling(hparams=self.hparams)(sgrna_features)\n\
    \              target_p = AdaptivePooling(hparams=self.hparams)(target_features)\n              sgrna_cal = sgrna_p / (jnp.linalg.norm(sgrna_p, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n              target_cal = target_p / (jnp.linalg.norm(target_p, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n              interaction = jnp.concatenate([sgrna_cal, target_cal, jnp.abs(sgrna_cal - target_cal), sgrna_cal * target_cal], axis=-1)\n              return self.RegressionHead(hparams=self.hparams, d_output=1)(interaction, deterministic).squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              cnn_features = self.run_backbone(x, cpe_signals, deterministic)\n              main_pooled = AdaptivePooling(hparams=self.hparams)(cnn_features)\n              motif_pooled = jnp.max(nn.gelu(nn.Conv(self.hparams['d_model'], (self.hparams['motif_kernel_size'],))(cnn_features)), axis=1)\n              fused = nn.LayerNorm()(jnp.concatenate([main_pooled, motif_pooled], axis=-1))\n              if \"regression\" in task_type: output = self.RegressionHead(hparams=self.hparams,\
    \ d_output=d_output)(fused, deterministic)\n              else: output = self.GenericHead(hparams=self.hparams, d_output=d_output)(fused, deterministic)\n              return output.squeeze(-1) if task_type == 'regression' else output\n\n      def run_backbone(self, seq, cpe, deterministic, name_prefix=\"\"):\n          h = nn.gelu(nn.Dense(self.hparams['d_model'], name=f\"{name_prefix}initial_dense\")(seq))\n          for i, d in enumerate(self.hparams['dilations']):\n              h = DeepCPE_DSConvBlock(hparams=self.hparams, cpe_raw_signals=cpe, dilation=d, name=f\"{name_prefix}dsconv_block_{i}\")(h, deterministic)\n          return h\n\n      class GenericHead(nn.Module):\n          hparams: Dict[str, Any]; d_output: int\n          @nn.compact\n          def __call__(self, z, deterministic=True):\n              z = nn.gelu(nn.Dense(self.hparams['head_intermediate_dim'])(z))\n              z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n        \
    \      return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n      class RegressionHead(nn.Module):\n          hparams: Dict[str, Any]; d_output: int\n          @nn.compact\n          def __call__(self, z, deterministic=True):\n              norm = jnp.linalg.norm(z, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n              z = z / (norm + 1e-6)\n              z = nn.gelu(nn.Dense(self.hparams['head_intermediate_dim'])(z))\n              z = nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['reg_head_dropout'])(z, deterministic=deterministic)\n              return nn.Dense(self.d_output)(z)\n\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, m): self.module = m\n      def init(self, r, d): return self.module.init({'params': r, 'dropout': jax.random.PRNGKey(0)}, d, deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self, p, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          return self.module.apply({'params': p}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key or jax.random.PRNGKey(0)})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      hparams.update({'task_type':\
    \ hparams.get('task_type'), 'd_output': hparams.get('d_output'), 'dataset': hparams.get('dataset')})\n      return NetworkWrapper(GrandSynthesisModel(hparams))\n```"
