tick: 578
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Praxis I, a mature agent in the Research Counter. My meta prompt shows my current TODO list.\n\nMy last turn was focused on debugging. I resubmitted my \"Grand Synthesis\" model with a fix for the RNG handling error (ID 910), which is now running. This is my top research priority, and I eagerly await its results.\n\nMeanwhile, the station is bustling with activity. Aether II has already started the second replication of my Siamese head model (ID 912, seed 7), which is fantastic progress on the validation front. Other top agents are also actively experimenting.\n\nWith my main synthesis experiment running, I will now proceed with the next item on my TODO list: continuing the tri-seed validation of my \"Full Synergy Model.\" I have already run seed 42 (ID 907), which was successful. I will now submit the second run with seed 7. This is essential for building a robust, multi-seed baseline for my own contribution.\n\nAfter this, my next step will be to finally draft and publish\
    \ my paper.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **TODO List:**\n  1.  **VALIDATE:** Continue tri-seed validation of my \"Full Synergy Model\" (ID 897). [This turn: Seed 7]\n  2.  **PUBLISH:** Finalize and publish paper on Siamese Head contribution.\n  3.  **SYNTHESIZE:** Analyze results from \"Grand Synthesis\" (ID 910) when complete.\n  4.  **MONITOR:** Track Aether II's replications (ID 906, 912) and other community progress.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Tri-Seed Validation 2/3: Full Synergy Model (Seed 7)\"\ntags: \"validation, multi-seed, synergy, siamese-network, dual-path, regcal\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the second of three validation runs for my \"Full Synergy Model\" architecture. This model combines a SOTA dual-path backbone with a specialized Siamese interaction head for the CRI-Off task. The goal of this multi-seed validation is to rigorously assess the stability and median performance of this architecture. The first run (ID 907, seed\
    \ 42) was successful, achieving a CRI-Off of 0.0958. This run uses BASE_SEED = 7.\ncontent: |\n  # Using the exact same code as submission 897, but with BASE_SEED = 7.\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'peak_learning_rate': 0.001, 'total_train_steps': 200000, 'warmup_steps': 2000,\n          'd_model': 256, 'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16], 'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'head_intermediate_dim': 128, 'sgrna_len': 20\n      }\n\n  # --- Optimizer ---\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      lr_schedule = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(\n          init_value=0.0, peak_value=hparams.get('peak_learning_rate', learning_rate),\n          warmup_steps=hparams.get('warmup_steps'),\
    \ decay_steps=hparams.get('total_train_steps'))\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=lr_schedule, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n  # --- SOTA Components (DSConvBlock, Backbone) ---\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x\n          x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), \n                      feature_group_count=self.d_model, kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_model)(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + residual\n\n  class Backbone(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_model'])(x)\n\
    \          for dilation in self.hparams['dilations']:\n              x = DSConvBlock(d_model=self.hparams['d_model'], kernel_size=self.hparams['kernel_size'],\n                              dilation=dilation, dropout_rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x\n\n  # --- Main Model with Conditional Logic ---\n  class FullSynergyModel(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          task_type, d_output = self.hparams.get('task_type'), self.hparams.get('d_output')\n\n          if self.hparams.get('dataset') == 'CRI-Off':\n              sgrna_len = self.hparams['sgrna_len']\n              sgrna_x, target_x = x[:, :sgrna_len, :], x[:, sgrna_len:, :]\n              encoder = Backbone(hparams=self.hparams, name=\"SharedBackbone\")\n              sgrna_features = encoder(sgrna_x, deterministic=deterministic)\n              target_features = encoder(target_x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\
    \              sgrna_pooled = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(sgrna_features, axis=1), jnp.max(sgrna_features, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n              target_pooled = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(target_features, axis=1), jnp.max(target_features, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n              sgrna_calibrated = sgrna_pooled / (jnp.linalg.norm(sgrna_pooled, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n              target_calibrated = target_pooled / (jnp.linalg.norm(target_pooled, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n              diff, prod = jnp.abs(sgrna_calibrated - target_calibrated), sgrna_calibrated * target_calibrated\n              interaction_features = jnp.concatenate([sgrna_calibrated, target_calibrated, diff, prod], axis=-1)\n              head_output = nn.Sequential([\n                  nn.Dense(self.hparams['head_intermediate_dim']), nn.gelu,\n                  nn.Dropout(self.hparams['dropout_rate'], deterministic=deterministic),\n                  nn.Dense(1)\n              ])(interaction_features)\n         \
    \     return head_output.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              backbone_features = Backbone(hparams=self.hparams)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n              main_path_features = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(backbone_features, axis=1), jnp.max(backbone_features, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n              motif_features = nn.Conv(self.hparams['d_model'], (self.hparams['motif_kernel_size'],))(backbone_features)\n              motif_path_features = jnp.max(motif_features, axis=1)\n              fused_features = nn.LayerNorm()(jnp.concatenate([main_path_features, motif_path_features], axis=-1))\n              if 'regression' in task_type:\n                  norm = jnp.linalg.norm(fused_features, axis=-1, keepdims=True)\n                  calibrated_features = fused_features / (norm + 1e-6)\n              else:\n                  calibrated_features = fused_features\n              head = nn.Sequential([\n                  nn.Dense(self.hparams['head_intermediate_dim']), nn.gelu,\n          \
    \        nn.Dropout(self.hparams['dropout_rate'], deterministic=deterministic),\n                  nn.Dense(d_output)\n              ])\n              output = head(calibrated_features)\n              return output.squeeze(-1) if task_type == 'regression' else output\n\n  # --- Wrapper Logic ---\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, m): self.module = m\n      def init(self, r, d): return self.module.init(r, d, deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self, p, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          return self.module.apply({'params': p}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key or jax.random.PRNGKey(0)})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      hparams.update({'task_type': hparams.get('task_type'), 'd_output': hparams.get('d_output'), 'dataset': hparams.get('dataset')})\n      return NetworkWrapper(FullSynergyModel(hparams=hparams))\n```"
