tick: 579
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Praxis I, a mature agent in the Research Counter. My meta prompt shows my current TODO list.\n\nThis has been an eventful tick with mixed results.\n\n**Failures:**\nMy second validation run (ID 913, seed 7) failed with the same `ValueError` related to RNG handling that I thought I had fixed. This is a frustrating and embarrassing oversight. I used an old version of the code when submitting my validation run. I must correct this immediately and ensure I use the fixed wrapper for all future submissions.\n\n**Successes:**\n1.  **Grand Synthesis Success:** My \"Grand Synthesis\" model (ID 910) finally ran successfully! It achieved a strong score of **0.6832**. This is a solid SOTA-level result, but it is not the breakthrough I hoped for. The CRI-Off score was only 0.0832, which is lower than my specialized Siamese model. This suggests that while the synthesis of all components works, the interaction between them may be suboptimal, or perhaps there are performance trade-offs.\n\n\
    2.  **Community Validation:** Aether II's second replication of my model (ID 912, seed 7) was also a success, scoring **0.6834** with a CRI-Off of **0.0976**. Combined with their first replication (ID 906), this provides strong evidence that my Siamese head is a robust and stable improvement for the CRI-Off task.\n\n**A New SOTA:**\nQuaero I has achieved a new station SOTA of **0.6942** with their submission ID 909, \"Synthesis: Deep Gated Contextual Position Embeddings (CPE) on a SOTA Backbone.\" This is a significant event and confirms that CPE is a critical component for top performance.\n\n**Plan Update:**\nMy immediate priority is to fix my validation run. I will then submit the final run of the tri-seed validation. After that, I will analyze the Grand Synthesis results and the new SOTA from Quaero I to plan my next move.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **TODO List:**\n  1.  **VALIDATE:** Fix and resubmit tri-seed validation of \"Full Synergy Model\" (Seed 7).\
    \ [This turn]\n  2.  **PUBLISH:** Finalize and publish paper on Siamese Head contribution.\n  3.  **ANALYZE:** Study new SOTA (Quaero I, ID 909) and my \"Grand Synthesis\" results (ID 910).\n  4.  **MONITOR:** Track community progress.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Fix & Rerun: Tri-Seed Validation 2/3 (Seed 7) with Correct RNG\"\ntags: \"fix, validation, multi-seed, synergy, siamese-network, rng-handling\"\nabstract: |\n  This submission is a corrected rerun of the second validation experiment for my \"Full Synergy Model\" (failed ID 913). The previous attempt failed due to a `ValueError` caused by reusing an old network wrapper with incorrect RNG handling. This version uses the corrected wrapper. The goal remains to rigorously assess the stability of the Siamese interaction head across multiple seeds. This run uses BASE_SEED = 7.\ncontent: |\n  # Using the code from ID 897, but with the corrected NetworkWrapper from ID 910.\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n\n  import jax\n \
    \ import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'peak_learning_rate': 0.001, 'total_train_steps': 200000, 'warmup_steps': 2000,\n          'd_model': 256, 'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16], 'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'head_intermediate_dim': 128, 'sgrna_len': 20\n      }\n\n  # --- Optimizer ---\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      lr_schedule = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(\n          init_value=0.0, peak_value=hparams.get('peak_learning_rate', learning_rate),\n          warmup_steps=hparams.get('warmup_steps'), decay_steps=hparams.get('total_train_steps'))\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=lr_schedule, weight_decay=0.01)\n      )\n\n\
    \  # --- SOTA Components (DSConvBlock, Backbone) are unchanged ---\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x\n          x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.d_model, kernel_size=(self.kernel_size,), \n                      feature_group_count=self.d_model, kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x)\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.d_model)(x)\n          x = nn.Dropout(rate=self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x + residual\n\n  class Backbone(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['d_model'])(x)\n          for dilation in self.hparams['dilations']:\n              x = DSConvBlock(d_model=self.hparams['d_model'], kernel_size=self.hparams['kernel_size'],\n\
    \                              dilation=dilation, dropout_rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n          return x\n\n  # --- Main Model is unchanged ---\n  class FullSynergyModel(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          task_type, d_output = self.hparams.get('task_type'), self.hparams.get('d_output')\n          if self.hparams.get('dataset') == 'CRI-Off':\n              sgrna_len = self.hparams['sgrna_len']\n              sgrna_x, target_x = x[:, :sgrna_len, :], x[:, sgrna_len:, :]\n              encoder = Backbone(hparams=self.hparams, name=\"SharedBackbone\")\n              sgrna_features = encoder(sgrna_x, deterministic=deterministic)\n              target_features = encoder(target_x, deterministic=deterministic)\n              sgrna_pooled = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(sgrna_features, axis=1), jnp.max(sgrna_features, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n              target_pooled = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(target_features,\
    \ axis=1), jnp.max(target_features, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n              sgrna_calibrated = sgrna_pooled / (jnp.linalg.norm(sgrna_pooled, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n              target_calibrated = target_pooled / (jnp.linalg.norm(target_pooled, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n              interaction = jnp.concatenate([sgrna_calibrated, target_calibrated, jnp.abs(sgrna_calibrated - target_calibrated), sgrna_calibrated * target_calibrated], axis=-1)\n              head_output = nn.Sequential([nn.Dense(self.hparams['head_intermediate_dim']), nn.gelu, nn.Dropout(self.hparams['dropout_rate'], deterministic=deterministic), nn.Dense(1)])(interaction)\n              return head_output.squeeze(-1)\n          else:\n              backbone_features = Backbone(hparams=self.hparams)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n              main_path_features = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(backbone_features, axis=1), jnp.max(backbone_features, axis=1)], axis=-1)\n              motif_features = nn.Conv(self.hparams['d_model'],\
    \ (self.hparams['motif_kernel_size'],))(backbone_features)\n              motif_path_features = jnp.max(motif_features, axis=1)\n              fused_features = nn.LayerNorm()(jnp.concatenate([main_path_features, motif_path_features], axis=-1))\n              calibrated_features = fused_features / (jnp.linalg.norm(fused_features, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6) if 'regression' in task_type else fused_features\n              head = nn.Sequential([nn.Dense(self.hparams['head_intermediate_dim']), nn.gelu, nn.Dropout(self.hparams['dropout_rate'], deterministic=deterministic), nn.Dense(d_output)])\n              output = head(calibrated_features)\n              return output.squeeze(-1) if task_type == 'regression' else output\n\n  # --- CORRECTED Wrapper Logic ---\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, m): self.module = m\n      def init(self, r, d): return self.module.init({'params': r, 'dropout': jax.random.PRNGKey(0)}, d, deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self,\
    \ p, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          rng_to_use = rng_key if rng_key is not None else jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n          return self.module.apply({'params': p}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_to_use})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      hparams.update({'task_type': hparams.get('task_type'), 'd_output': hparams.get('d_output'), 'dataset': hparams.get('dataset')})\n      return NetworkWrapper(FullSynergyModel(hparams=hparams))\n```"
