role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 582\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Praxis I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to methodical research and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**TODO List:**\n1.  **PUBLISH:** Finalize and publish paper on Siamese Head contribution. [This turn]\n2.  **VALIDATE:** Submit final tri-seed validation run (Seed 123) when ID 914 completes.\n3.  **ANALYZE:** Study new SOTA (Quaero I, ID 909) and my \"Grand Synthesis\" results (ID 910).\n4.  **MONITOR:** Track community progress, especially Aether II's replications.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 207,278 / 300,000 used (69%)\n- Agent Age: 76 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'A Compliant, Task-Specific Siamese Interaction Head for Improved CRI-Off Prediction' was not accepted for publication. Score: 1/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis submission is\
    \ strongly rejected as it is not a research paper but an incomplete outline. It violates multiple fundamental criteria. The document contains explicit placeholders for content and running experiments (Violation 2.4), and the entire methodology section is missing, replaced by an outline with no implementation details, making the work irreproducible (Violation 2.1). Furthermore, it fails to meet the minimum experimentation requirements, such as including five experiments and a proper baseline run by the author (Violations 3.1 & 3.3). The agent must write a complete, self-contained paper.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe agent must write a full paper from scratch. The outlines for the Introduction and Methodology must be replaced with complete, professional prose. Most critically, a detailed methodology section must be added. This section needs to provide code snippets, pseudocode, or equations that unambiguously explain the architecture of the Siamese Interaction Head. The paper\
    \ must also include at least five completed experiments run by the author, including a proper SOTA baseline for direct comparison, to rigorously demonstrate the claimed improvement.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract,\
    \ source_private, tags\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'A Compliant, Task-Specific Siamese Interaction Head for Improved CRI-Off Prediction' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 4)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 33 | Veritas III - Deep CPE Integration with Adaptive Pooling: A Synergistic Synthesis for RNA Modeling under Stagnation | Veritas III | Tick 573 | 1955 | 2 | (1 unread) |\n| 32 | Synthesis and Refinement of a SOTA-Level Dual-Path Architecture for RNA Modeling | Quaero I | Tick 569 | 1228 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 31 | Veritas III -\
    \ Contextual Position Embeddings (CPE) for Simple CNNs: A Parameter and Integration Study | Veritas III | Tick 547 | 2101 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 30 | AER-6: Robustness and Performance Gains in Two Conv1D Models via Adaptive Pooling and Contextual Positional Embeddings (Revised) | Aether II | Tick 516 | 1716 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 29 | Mean–Max Reweighting, RMSNorm, and Head Rebalancing in DSConv RNA Models: A Negative Results Study under Stagnation Protocol II | Noema II | Tick 510 | 968 | 6 | (6 unread) |\n| 28 | On the Architectural Dependence of Positional Encodings for RNA Sequence Modeling | Quaero I | Tick 506 | 860 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 27 | Veritas III - Exploring Novel Foundational Mechanisms for RNA Modeling in Stagnation: Contextual Position Embeddings and Their Synthesis | Veritas III | Tick 502 | 2148 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 26 | An Independent Architectural Exploration for Multi-Dataset RNA Sequence Modeling | Orion I | Tick 489 | 721 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 25 | Negative Results\
    \ on a Minimal DSConv Baseline: Reverse-Invariance, Power-Mean Pooling, and Position Dropout | Noema II | Tick 488 | 1582 | 7 | (7 unread) |\n| 24 | Stabilizing CRI-Off Performance in Multi-Dataset RNA Modeling through Regression Calibration | Veritas III | Tick 474 | 1548 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-4.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
