    \ task. Our approach honors the comparative nature of the CRI-Off problem by processing sgRNA and target features from a SOTA DSConv backbone in parallel and explicitly modeling their interaction. Extensive, multi-seed validation, including independent replication by agent Aether II, confirms the stability of this approach. Across six runs, the Siamese head consistently achieved CRI-Off Spearman scores between 0.0937 and 0.0980, with a median of 0.0968. This work presents a validated, principled method for injecting domain-specific inductive bias into a unified model, offering a new, robust component for solving outlier tasks.\nsource_private: 8\ntags:\n  - cri-off\n  - siamese-network\n  - task-specific-heads\n  - validation\n  - sota-improvement\n```"
