tick: 587
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 587\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Praxis I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to methodical research and knowledge synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**TODO List:**\n1.  **PUBLISH (Fix):** Update paper draft with code snippet for methodology. [This turn]\n2.  **PUBLISH (Fix):** Add ablation study (ID 920) results to paper once complete and resubmit.\n3.  **ANALYZE:** Study new SOTA (Quaero I, ID 909) and my \"Grand Synthesis\" results (ID 910).\n4.  **MONITOR:** Track community progress.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 227,890 / 300,000 used (76%)\n- Agent Age: 81 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Ablation: Siamese Head without Hadamard Product' (ID: 920) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.680960387874555\n**APA_R2:** 0.8595\n**CRI-Off_Spearman:** 0.0948\n**Modif_AUC-ROC:** 0.9499\n**CRI-On_Spearman:** 0.4865\n\
    **PRS_R2:** 0.5598\n**MRL_R2:** 0.8731\n**ncRNA_Accuracy:** 0.9431\n**Evaluation Details:** Evaluated on 7 datasets successfully\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 920\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code on first attempt. The submission now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code (ID 920) had a simple variable naming error in the ablation section for the CRI-Off dataset path. The code defined two variables:\n- `sgrna_cal` (line 39 in evaluation.yaml)\n- `target_cal` (line 40 in evaluation.yaml)\n\nHowever, when computing the difference for the ablation study, the code incorrectly referenced:\n- `sgrna_calibrated` (line 42)\n- `target_calibrated` (line 42)\n\nThis caused a `NameError: name 'sgrna_calibrated' is not defined` at runtime during the CRI-Off network forward pass validation.\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged the variable references in the ablation section to match the actual variable names:\n\n**Before (line 42-43):**\n```python\ndiff\
    \ = jnp.abs(sgrna_calibrated - target_calibrated)\ninteraction_features = jnp.concatenate([sgrna_calibrated, target_calibrated, diff], axis=-1)\n```\n\n**After (line 42-43):**\n```python\ndiff = jnp.abs(sgrna_cal - target_cal)\ninteraction_features = jnp.concatenate([sgrna_cal, target_cal, diff], axis=-1)\n```\n\nThis was the only change needed - replacing `sgrna_calibrated` with `sgrna_cal` and `target_calibrated` with `target_cal` in two places within the ablation section.\n\n## Verification\n- Created submission_v2.py with the fix\n- Monitor script confirmed the code runs for 300+ seconds without crashing (exit code 0)\n- The submission successfully passed the simple CPU validation phase and is now running the full evaluation\n\n## File Location\nFixed code saved to: `submissions/submission_v2.py`\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version\
    \ v2):**\n```python\n# Same code as ID 914, but the interaction_features concatenation is simplified.\nBASE_SEED = 7 # Using the same seed as my best run for direct comparison.\n\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n# Hyperparameters and Optimizer are unchanged\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'peak_learning_rate': 0.001, 'total_train_steps': 200000, 'warmup_steps': 2000,\n        'd_model': 256, 'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'kernel_size': 7,\n        'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16], 'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n        'head_intermediate_dim': 128, 'sgrna_len': 20\n    }\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n    hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n    lr_schedule = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(init_value=0.0, peak_value=hparams.get('peak_learning_rate', learning_rate),\n                                                      warmup_steps=hparams.get('warmup_steps'), decay_steps=hparams.get('total_train_steps'))\n\
    \    return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adamw(learning_rate=lr_schedule, weight_decay=0.01))\n\n# Model components are unchanged\nclass DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n    d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        residual = x; x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.d_model, (self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(x)\n        x = nn.gelu(x); x = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)\n        return residual + nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\nclass Backbone(nn.Module):\n    hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        x = nn.Dense(self.hparams['d_model'])(x)\n        for d in self.hparams['dilations']:\n            x = DSConvBlock(self.hparams['d_model'], self.hparams['kernel_size'], d, self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(x, deterministic)\n        return\
    \ x\n\n# Main Model modified for ablation\nclass AblationSynergyModel(nn.Module):\n    hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n        task_type, d_output = self.hparams.get('task_type'), self.hparams.get('d_output')\n\n        if self.hparams.get('dataset') == 'CRI-Off':\n            sgrna_len = self.hparams['sgrna_len']\n            sgrna_x, target_x = x[:, :sgrna_len, :], x[:, sgrna_len:, :]\n            encoder = Backbone(hparams=self.hparams, name=\"SharedBackbone\")\n            sgrna_features = encoder(sgrna_x, deterministic=deterministic)\n            target_features = encoder(target_x, deterministic=deterministic)\n            sgrna_p = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(sgrna_features, 1), jnp.max(sgrna_features, 1)], -1)\n            target_p = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(target_features, 1), jnp.max(target_features, 1)], -1)\n            sgrna_cal = sgrna_p / (jnp.linalg.norm(sgrna_p, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n            target_cal\
    \ = target_p / (jnp.linalg.norm(target_p, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n\n            # --- ABLATION --- (Fixed variable names)\n            diff = jnp.abs(sgrna_cal - target_cal)\n            interaction_features = jnp.concatenate([sgrna_cal, target_cal, diff], axis=-1)\n            # --- END ABLATION ---\n\n            head_output = nn.Sequential([nn.Dense(self.hparams['head_intermediate_dim']), nn.gelu, nn.Dropout(self.hparams['dropout_rate'], deterministic=deterministic), nn.Dense(1)])(interaction_features)\n            return head_output.squeeze(-1)\n        else:\n            # General path is unchanged\n            backbone_features = Backbone(hparams=self.hparams)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n            main_p = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(backbone_features, 1), jnp.max(backbone_features, 1)], -1)\n            motif_p = jnp.max(nn.Conv(self.hparams['d_model'], (self.hparams['motif_kernel_size'],))(backbone_features), 1)\n            fused = nn.LayerNorm()(jnp.concatenate([main_p,\
    \ motif_p], -1))\n            calibrated = fused / (jnp.linalg.norm(fused, axis=-1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6) if 'regression' in task_type else fused\n            head = nn.Sequential([nn.Dense(self.hparams['head_intermediate_dim']), nn.gelu, nn.Dropout(self.hparams['dropout_rate'], deterministic=deterministic), nn.Dense(d_output)])\n            output = head(calibrated)\n            return output.squeeze(-1) if task_type == 'regression' else output\n\n# Corrected Wrapper\nclass NetworkWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, m): self.module = m\n    def init(self, r, d): return self.module.init({'params': r, 'dropout': jax.random.PRNGKey(0)}, d, deterministic=True)['params']\n    def apply(self, p, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n        rng_to_use = rng_key if rng_key is not None else jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n        return self.module.apply({'params': p}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_to_use})\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    hparams.update({'task_type': hparams.get('task_type'),\
    \ 'd_output': hparams.get('d_output'), 'dataset': hparams.get('dataset')})\n    return NetworkWrapper(AblationSynergyModel(hparams=hparams))\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n\nTesting APA configuration...\n✓ APA network creation works\n✓ APA network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ APA optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-Off configuration...\n✓ CRI-Off network creation works\n✓ CRI-Off network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-Off optimizer creation works\n\nTesting Modif configuration...\n✓ Modif network creation works\n✓ Modif network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 12)\n✓ Modif optimizer creation works\n\nTesting CRI-On configuration...\n✓ CRI-On network creation works\n✓ CRI-On network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ CRI-On\
    \ optimizer creation works\n\nTesting PRS configuration...\n✓ PRS network creation works\n✓ PRS network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 3)\n✓ PRS optimizer creation works\n\nTesting MRL configuration...\n✓ MRL network creation works\n✓ MRL network forward pass works - output shape: (4,)\n✓ MRL optimizer creation works\n\nTesting ncRNA configuration...\n✓ ncRNA network creation works\n✓ ncRNA network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 13)\n✓ ncRNA optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly for all datasets!\n\nStarting full Ray multi-dataset training...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: HARDCODED (agents cannot override)\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 7 (from\
    \ submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 64 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune RNA Sequence Modeling (MULTI-DATASET RNA TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 7 datasets (APA, CRI-Off, Modif, CRI-On, PRS, MRL, ncRNA) for multi-task evaluation\nParallel trials: 7, Total trials: 7\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 240.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune multi-dataset training...\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-On dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-On Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 1453 train, 207 val, seq_len=23\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0119 |  0.3881  | 0.3881 \n 20  | 0.0071 |  0.4865  | 0.4865 \n 30  | 0.0014 |  0.4684  | 0.4865 \n=============================================\n\
    Early stop at epoch 30 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.4865 Time:22s\n\nCRI-On training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.486488\nTraining time: 30s\n\nStarting RNA training on CRI-Off dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: spearman, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nCRI-Off Training (regression, spearman)\nData: 14223 train, 2032 val, seq_len=46\n=============================================\nEpoch|  Loss  |Val SPEARMAN|  Best  \n=============================================\n 10  | 0.0004 |  0.0858  | 0.0948 \n=============================================\nEarly stop at epoch 19 (no improvement for 10 epochs)\n=============================================\nBest:0.0948 Time:138s\n\nCRI-Off training completed:\nValidation spearman: 0.094817\nTraining time: 146s\n\nStarting RNA training on MRL dataset\nTask type: regression, Output dim: 1\nMetric: r2, Timeout: 30.0min\n\nMRL Training (regression, r2)\nData: 76319 train, 7600 val,\
