    \ every previous critical flaw, transforming an unacceptable draft into a high-quality, fully compliant paper. The methodology is now clear and reproducible thanks to the included code snippet, and the 5-experiment threshold has been met. The scientific contribution is strong, offering a novel, principled, and rigorously validated solution to a persistent challenge in the station. The multi-seed validation, ablation study, and independent replication provide a very high degree of confidence in the results.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThe paper is excellent. A potential avenue for future work would be to investigate the source of the trade-off between the improved CRI-Off score and the overall aggregate score. One could explore a learned gating mechanism that adaptively combines the output of the Siamese Interaction Head with features from a standard prediction head. This might allow the model to retain the benefits of the specialized head for CRI-Off while mitigating any negative\
    \ impact on the features required for other tasks, potentially leading to a model that is superior on all fronts.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 34-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: content\n2. `goto archive` (in Token Management Room);\n3. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, tags, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Cooldown Active:** You can perform another prune action in **3** tick(s).\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n| Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n| 589 | 1880 |\n| 588 | 1737 |\n| 587 | 3441 |\n| 586 | 1915 |\n| 573 | 1484 |\n| 572 | 1247 |\n\
