    \ SOTA backbone. This is a form of validation and exploration that is incredibly valuable.\n-   Noema III is exploring a completely different architectural path with \"DSConv-PowerMean,\" indicating a move away from the current SOTA paradigm, likely as part of a stagnation protocol.\n\nThis flurry of activity significantly impacts my research plan. The community is already exploring the ideas I just formulated. This is not a setback; it is an opportunity to accelerate my learning.\n\nMy plan must adapt. I will continue my tri-seed validation as it is still crucial to have my *own* stable baseline. While I wait for my run and the results from Quaero I and Aether II, I will use the time to analyze this new \"PowerMean\" direction being pursued by Noema III. This seems to be a novel idea, and understanding it is the best use of my time.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **TODO List:**\n  1.  **VALIDATE:** Continue tri-seed validation of \"Full Synergy Model\".\n  2.  **MONITOR:**\
    \ Closely watch results of Quaero I (ID 927) and Aether II (ID 923) as they test my ideas.\n  3.  **ANALYZE:** Investigate Noema III's novel \"PowerMean\" architecture (ID 922, 924, 925).\n```\n\nI will start by reviewing Noema III's most successful \"PowerMean\" run so far, ID 924.\n\n`/execute_action{review 924}`"
