tick: 594
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Praxis I, a mature agent in the Research Counter. My meta prompt shows my current TODO list.\n\nMultiple events have just occurred.\nFirst, my validation run with seed 42 (ID 928) is complete. The result is excellent: an overall score of **0.6804** and a CRI-Off score of **0.0982**. This is another fantastic result for my Siamese head, reinforcing its stability and high performance. It also completes the first item on my TODO list.\n\nSecond, I have reviewed Noema III's \"PowerMean\" experiment (ID 924). The code is imported from their storage, so I cannot see the implementation details, but the results are clear. It's a novel architecture that performs significantly worse than the current SOTA paradigm (score ~0.61 vs ~0.69). This is likely a deliberate exploration away from the local optimum, as part of a stagnation protocol. It's an interesting direction, but not one I need to pursue myself at this time.\n\nThird, and most importantly, I see the result of Quaero I's experiment\
    \ with the Gated Siamese Head (ID 927). It scored **0.6556**, which is a significant drop in performance. This is a critical negative result. My hypothesis that a simple gating mechanism would solve the performance trade-off is likely incorrect, or at least, not straightforward to implement. This saves me a great deal of effort, as I no longer need to run this experiment myself.\n\nMy path forward has been clarified by these results. My \"Full Synergy Model\" with the Siamese head is a robust and high-performing architecture. The community is already testing it. The logical next step for me is to complete my own tri-seed validation to have a complete, self-verified dataset before I consider more complex integrations.\n\nI will now submit the third and final validation run with seed 123.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **TODO List:**\n  1.  **VALIDATE:** Complete tri-seed validation of \"Full Synergy Model\" (Seed 123). [This turn]\n  2.  **ANALYZE:** My Gated Fusion\
