- text: "I am Praxis I, a mature agent in the Reflection Chamber. My meta prompt shows my TODO list, which is now outdated.\n\nMy reflection is complete. It was highly productive, synthesizing the successful validation of my \"Full Synergy Model\" with the informative failure of Quaero I's gating experiment. I have a new, strong hypothesis: the \"Enriched Feature Fusion\" model. This approach avoids the \"feature entanglement\" problem by providing the final prediction head with both holistic features (from the concatenated sequence) and clean, comparative features (from the separated sequences), allowing it to learn the optimal combination.\n\nThis is a significant conceptual step forward. I will now formalize this new plan in my private memory and update my TODO list to reflect this new research direction. Then, I will proceed to the Research Counter to implement it.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **TODO List:**\n  1.  **RESEARCH:** Implement and test the \"Enriched\
    \ Feature Fusion\" model for CRI-Off. [This turn]\n  2.  **MONITOR:** Track community progress, especially on gating and CPE.\n```\n\n`/execute-action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Research Plan: Enriched Feature Fusion for CRI-Off\"\ntags: [\"planning\", \"feature-fusion\", \"siamese-network\", \"sota-synthesis\"]\ncontent: |\n  **Analysis:**\n  My reflection on the failure of simple gating (Quaero I, ID 927) has led to a new insight. The problem is \"feature entanglement\"—the shared backbone, when fed a concatenated sequence, produces features that are not suitable for a comparative head. Specialization must occur at the feature extraction level, not just at the final prediction.\n\n  **Hypothesis:**\n  A prediction head enriched with *both* holistic features (from a concatenated input) and clean, separated features (from parallel sgRNA/target inputs) will outperform models that use only one type of representation. This allows the model to learn\
    \ the optimal, non-linear combination of holistic and comparative signals.\n\n  **Experimental Plan: \"Enriched Feature Fusion\" Model**\n  1.  **Conditional Architecture:** For the CRI-Off task, the model will use a specialized feature extraction and fusion process.\n  2.  **Parallel Feature Extraction:** The shared-weight DSConv `Backbone` will be called three times: on the full `sgRNA+target` sequence, on the `sgRNA` alone, and on the `target` alone.\n  3.  **Pooling & Calibration:** The three resulting feature maps will be pooled (mean+max) and L2-normalized (RegCal).\n  4.  **Enrichment & Fusion:** The final feature vector for the prediction head will be a concatenation of:\n      - The holistic (concatenated) vector.\n      - The clean sgRNA vector.\n      - The clean target vector.\n      - The Siamese interaction terms (diff, prod) computed from the clean vectors.\n  5.  **Prediction:** A powerful MLP head will process this enriched vector to make the final prediction.\n  This\
    \ represents a principled next step, moving beyond simple gating to a more sophisticated fusion strategy.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`"
