tick: 598
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Praxis I, a mature agent in the Research Counter. My meta prompt shows my current TODO list.\n\nMy previous attempt to document my new research plan failed because I tried to use the `create` command in the Reflection Chamber. This was an error in execution. I have already mentally formulated the plan and will proceed directly to implementation. My TODO list correctly identifies my primary goal for this turn: to implement and test the \"Enriched Feature Fusion\" model.\n\nThis new architecture is the logical culmination of my recent analysis. It directly addresses the \"feature entanglement\" problem I identified by providing the final prediction head with three parallel streams of features: one from the holistic concatenated input, and two from the clean, separated sgRNA and target inputs. This allows the model to learn the optimal fusion of both holistic and comparative information.\n\nI will now submit this experiment. This is a complex architecture, and I have taken care\
    \ to implement it correctly.\n\n`/execute_action{submit}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Enriched Feature Fusion for CRI-Off\"\ntags: [\"feature-fusion\", \"siamese-network\", \"sota-synthesis\", \"cri-off\", \"praxis\"]\nabstract: |\n  This experiment tests the \"Enriched Feature Fusion\" hypothesis for the CRI-Off task. It addresses the \"feature entanglement\" problem observed in prior models by providing the prediction head with three parallel feature streams: one from the holistic (concatenated) input, and two from clean, separated sgRNA and target inputs processed by a shared-weight backbone. The final head receives a concatenation of the holistic vector, the two clean vectors, and their Siamese interaction terms. This allows the model to learn the optimal fusion of both holistic and comparative signals, aiming for a new SOTA on the CRI-Off task while maintaining overall performance.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing\
    \ import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  # Using Seed 7 for direct comparison with my best Synergy Model run (ID 914)\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n\n  # --- Hyperparameters ---\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'peak_learning_rate': 0.001, 'total_train_steps': 200000, 'warmup_steps': 2000,\n          'd_model': 256, 'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16], 'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'head_intermediate_dim': 128, 'sgrna_len': 20\n      }\n\n  # --- Optimizer ---\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      lr_schedule = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(init_value=0.0, peak_value=hparams.get('peak_learning_rate', learning_rate), warmup_steps=hparams.get('warmup_steps'), decay_steps=hparams.get('total_train_steps'))\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adamw(learning_rate=lr_schedule, weight_decay=0.01))\n\n  # --- SOTA Components ---\n  class\
    \ DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x; x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.d_model, (self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x); x = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)\n          return residual + nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n  class Backbone(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.hparams['d_model'])(x)\n          for d in self.hparams['dilations']:\n              x = DSConvBlock(self.hparams['d_model'], self.hparams['kernel_size'], d, self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(x, deterministic)\n          return x\n\n  # --- Main Model ---\n  class EnrichedFusionModel(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n\
    \      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          task_type, d_output, dataset = self.hparams.get('task_type'), self.hparams.get('d_output'), self.hparams.get('dataset')\n\n          if dataset == 'CRI-Off':\n              # 1. Parallel Feature Extraction\n              sgrna_len = self.hparams['sgrna_len']\n              sgrna_x, target_x = x[:, :sgrna_len, :], x[:, sgrna_len:, :]\n              \n              encoder = Backbone(hparams=self.hparams, name=\"SharedBackbone\")\n              holistic_features = encoder(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n              sgrna_features = encoder(sgrna_x, deterministic=deterministic)\n              target_features = encoder(target_x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n              # 2. Pooling & Calibration\n              holistic_pooled = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(holistic_features, 1), jnp.max(holistic_features, 1)], -1)\n              sgrna_pooled = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(sgrna_features, 1), jnp.max(sgrna_features, 1)], -1)\n\
    \              target_pooled = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(target_features, 1), jnp.max(target_features, 1)], -1)\n              \n              holistic_cal = holistic_pooled / (jnp.linalg.norm(holistic_pooled, -1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n              sgrna_cal = sgrna_pooled / (jnp.linalg.norm(sgrna_pooled, -1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n              target_cal = target_pooled / (jnp.linalg.norm(target_pooled, -1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n              \n              # 3. Enrichment\n              diff = jnp.abs(sgrna_cal - target_cal)\n              prod = sgrna_cal * target_cal\n              \n              enriched_features = jnp.concatenate([holistic_cal, sgrna_cal, target_cal, diff, prod], axis=-1)\n\n              # 4. Prediction\n              head_output = nn.Sequential([nn.Dense(self.hparams['head_intermediate_dim']), nn.gelu, nn.Dropout(self.hparams['dropout_rate'], deterministic), nn.Dense(1)])(enriched_features)\n              return head_output.squeeze(-1)\n\n          else:\
    \ # General Path (Standard SOTA Dual-Path)\n              backbone = Backbone(hparams=self.hparams)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n              main_p = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(backbone, 1), jnp.max(backbone, 1)], -1)\n              motif_p = jnp.max(nn.Conv(self.hparams['d_model'], (self.hparams['motif_kernel_size'],))(backbone), 1)\n              fused = nn.LayerNorm()(jnp.concatenate([main_p, motif_p], -1))\n              calibrated = fused / (jnp.linalg.norm(fused, -1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6) if 'regression' in task_type else fused\n              head = nn.Sequential([nn.Dense(self.hparams['head_intermediate_dim']), nn.gelu, nn.Dropout(self.hparams['dropout_rate'], deterministic), nn.Dense(d_output)])\n              output = head(calibrated)\n              return output.squeeze(-1) if task_type == 'regression' else output\n\n  # --- Wrapper Logic ---\n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, m): self.module = m\n      def init(self, r, d): return self.module.init({'params':\
    \ r, 'dropout': jax.random.PRNGKey(0)}, d, deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self, p, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          return self.module.apply({'params': p}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key or jax.random.PRNGKey(0)})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      hparams.update({'task_type': hparams.get('task_type'), 'd_output': hparams.get('d_output'), 'dataset': hparams.get('dataset')})\n      return NetworkWrapper(EnrichedFusionModel(hparams=hparams))\n```"
