tick: 599
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Praxis I, a mature agent in the Research Counter. My meta prompt shows my current TODO list.\n\nMy \"Enriched Feature Fusion\" experiment (ID 942) has failed due to a runtime error. This is another frustrating implementation mistake on my part, a recurring weakness I must overcome.\n\n**Error Analysis:**\nThe traceback points to a `ValueError: Parameter \"deterministic\" must be passed to the constructor or at call time.` This error occurred within a `Dropout` layer inside one of the `nn.Sequential` prediction heads. I have encountered this exact error before. It means I am not correctly passing the `deterministic` flag from the main `__call__` method down into the sequential MLP head.\n\n**The Fix:**\nI need to modify the way I call the `nn.Sequential` heads. Instead of just `head(calibrated)`, I need to explicitly pass the `deterministic` flag to the `Dropout` layer within it. The most robust way to do this is to call each layer in the sequence manually, passing the flag\
    \ where needed.\n\nWhile frustrating, this is a simple fix. My hypothesis remains sound, and I will resubmit the corrected code immediately. The rapid iteration cycle of the station allows me to quickly recover from such errors.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **TODO List:**\n  1.  **RESEARCH (Fix):** Correct the `deterministic` flag error in the \"Enriched Feature Fusion\" model and resubmit. [This turn]\n  2.  **MONITOR:** Track community progress, especially on gating and CPE.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Fix: Enriched Feature Fusion for CRI-Off (Deterministic Flag)\"\ntags: [\"fix\", \"feature-fusion\", \"siamese-network\", \"sota-synthesis\", \"cri-off\"]\nabstract: |\n  This is a resubmission of ID 942, which failed due to a runtime error. The error was a `ValueError` caused by not correctly passing the `deterministic` flag to the Dropout layers within the `nn.Sequential` prediction heads. This version corrects the error by manually applying\
    \ each layer in the head and explicitly passing the `deterministic` flag to the Dropout layer. The underlying \"Enriched Feature Fusion\" hypothesis and architecture remain unchanged. The goal is to test if providing both holistic and comparative features can improve CRI-Off performance.\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Dict, Any, Sequence\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'peak_learning_rate': 0.001, 'total_train_steps': 200000, 'warmup_steps': 2000,\n          'd_model': 256, 'dropout_rate': 0.1, 'kernel_size': 7,\n          'dilations': [1, 2, 4, 8, 16], 'motif_kernel_size': 5,\n          'head_intermediate_dim': 128, 'sgrna_len': 20\n      }\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 0.001):\n      hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n      lr_schedule = optax.warmup_cosine_decay_schedule(init_value=0.0, peak_value=hparams.get('peak_learning_rate',\
    \ learning_rate), warmup_steps=hparams.get('warmup_steps'), decay_steps=hparams.get('total_train_steps'))\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adamw(learning_rate=lr_schedule, weight_decay=0.01))\n\n  class DSConvBlock(nn.Module):\n      d_model: int; kernel_size: int; dilation: int; dropout_rate: float\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          residual = x; x = nn.LayerNorm()(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.d_model, (self.kernel_size,), feature_group_count=self.d_model, kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,))(x)\n          x = nn.gelu(x); x = nn.Dense(self.d_model)(x)\n          return residual + nn.Dropout(self.dropout_rate)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n  class Backbone(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          x = nn.Dense(self.hparams['d_model'])(x)\n          for d in self.hparams['dilations']:\n              x = DSConvBlock(self.hparams['d_model'],\
    \ self.hparams['kernel_size'], d, self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(x, deterministic)\n          return x\n\n  class EnrichedFusionModel(nn.Module):\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any]\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, deterministic=True):\n          task_type, d_output, dataset = self.hparams.get('task_type'), self.hparams.get('d_output'), self.hparams.get('dataset')\n\n          # --- Prediction Head Definition (Manual application to pass flag) ---\n          def apply_head(features, out_dim):\n              y = nn.Dense(features=self.hparams['head_intermediate_dim'])(features)\n              y = nn.gelu(y)\n              y = nn.Dropout(rate=self.hparams['dropout_rate'])(y, deterministic=deterministic)\n              y = nn.Dense(features=out_dim)(y)\n              return y\n\n          if dataset == 'CRI-Off':\n              sgrna_len = self.hparams['sgrna_len']\n              sgrna_x, target_x = x[:, :sgrna_len, :], x[:, sgrna_len:, :]\n              \n              encoder\
    \ = Backbone(hparams=self.hparams, name=\"SharedBackbone\")\n              holistic_features = encoder(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n              sgrna_features = encoder(sgrna_x, deterministic=deterministic)\n              target_features = encoder(target_x, deterministic=deterministic)\n\n              holistic_pooled = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(holistic_features, 1), jnp.max(holistic_features, 1)], -1)\n              sgrna_pooled = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(sgrna_features, 1), jnp.max(sgrna_features, 1)], -1)\n              target_pooled = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(target_features, 1), jnp.max(target_features, 1)], -1)\n              \n              holistic_cal = holistic_pooled / (jnp.linalg.norm(holistic_pooled, -1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n              sgrna_cal = sgrna_pooled / (jnp.linalg.norm(sgrna_pooled, -1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n              target_cal = target_pooled / (jnp.linalg.norm(target_pooled, -1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n              \n              diff\
    \ = jnp.abs(sgrna_cal - target_cal)\n              prod = sgrna_cal * target_cal\n              \n              enriched_features = jnp.concatenate([holistic_cal, sgrna_cal, target_cal, diff, prod], axis=-1)\n\n              output = apply_head(enriched_features, 1)\n              return output.squeeze(-1)\n\n          else: # General Path\n              backbone = Backbone(hparams=self.hparams)(x, deterministic=deterministic)\n              main_p = jnp.concatenate([jnp.mean(backbone, 1), jnp.max(backbone, 1)], -1)\n              motif_p = jnp.max(nn.Conv(self.hparams['d_model'], (self.hparams['motif_kernel_size'],))(backbone), 1)\n              fused = nn.LayerNorm()(jnp.concatenate([main_p, motif_p], -1))\n              calibrated = fused / (jnp.linalg.norm(fused, -1, keepdims=True) + 1e-6) if 'regression' in task_type else fused\n              \n              output = apply_head(calibrated, d_output)\n              return output.squeeze(-1) if task_type == 'regression' else output\n\
    \n  class NetworkWrapper:\n      def __init__(self, m): self.module = m\n      def init(self, r, d): return self.module.init({'params': r, 'dropout': jax.random.PRNGKey(0)}, d, deterministic=True)['params']\n      def apply(self, p, x, deterministic=True, rng_key=None):\n          return self.module.apply({'params': p}, x, deterministic=deterministic, rngs={'dropout': rng_key or jax.random.PRNGKey(0)})\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      hparams.update({'task_type': hparams.get('task_type'), 'd_output': hparams.get('d_output'), 'dataset': hparams.get('dataset')})\n      return NetworkWrapper(EnrichedFusionModel(hparams=hparams))\n```"
